cmn2wa1fz001ijc3otlu4u94s	audit-risk-add	internal-audit	Risk Register	audit	{}	How do I add a new risk to the audit risk register?	How do I add a new risk to the audit risk register?\nCreate audit risk\nAdd risk manually\nNew risk entry audit\nRegister new audit risk\nAdd a new risk manually by filling out the risk details form including category, description, inherent/residual scoring, controls, and supporting evidence.\nNavigate to **Internal Audit** > **Risk Register**\nClick the **+ Add Risk Manually** button\nFill in the basic details: **Risk Name**, **Department**, **Section/Process**, **Sub-Process**, **Activity**, **Category**\nEnter the **Risk Description** with potential causes and impacts\nSet **Inherent Risk Scoring**: select Inherent Likelihood and Inherent Impact\nDefine **Controls**: enter Control Description and Control Effectiveness\nSet **Residual Risk Scoring**: select Residual Likelihood and Residual Impact\nAdd **Audit Information**: Creation Date (auto), Audit Comment, Status\nUpload **Evidence Files** by clicking or dragging files into the attachment area\nClick **Save** to add the risk to the register\nRisk ID is auto-generated (e.g., RID001) and cannot be edited\nInherent risk is assessed before controls; residual risk is assessed after controls\nControl Effectiveness options: Effective, Needs Improvement, Ineffective\nStatus options: Open, Under Review, Closed\nadd\ncreate\nnew\nrisk\nregister\nmanual\naudit	{0.004669189453125,0.052520751953125,0.0592041015625,-0.0252227783203125,-0.048309326171875,-0.01934814453125,-0.00537109375,-0.01473236083984375,-0.002904891967773438,0.03668212890625,-0.00591278076171875,-0.01209259033203125,0.0257568359375,-0.01059722900390625,0.0236053466796875,-0.0628662109375,0.0173797607421875,0.032073974609375,-0.01546478271484375,0.044464111328125,-0.002305984497070312,0.02960205078125,0.0256195068359375,-0.0165863037109375,-0.0283966064453125,0.00626373291015625,-0.01373291015625,-0.0239715576171875,-0.0261688