cmn2wa1gr001kjc3o4cwyiiao	audit-planning-create	internal-audit	Audit Planning	audit	{}	How do I create a new audit engagement?	How do I create a new audit engagement?\nAdd audit engagement\nNew audit plan\nCreate audit\nSchedule new audit\nPlan new audit\nCreate a new audit engagement by filling in the audit objectives, scope, responsible personnel, risks, and testing details.\nNavigate to **Internal Audit** > **Audit Planning**\nClick the **Add Engagement** button\nFill in the mandatory fields: **Engagement Title**, **Engagement Objective**, **Engagement Scope**\nSelect the **Department** being audited\n**Link Open Risks** in the selected department\nReview **Historical Risks** from the previous year for reference\nSelect the **Audit Rating** (High, Medium, Low) and **Audit Type** (Regular, Follow-up, Special)\nAssign the **Auditor** and **Auditee**\nSet the **Start Date** and **Target Date**\nUpload **Attachments** and **Workpapers**\nOptionally enter **Auditor's Initial Observation**\nFill in the **Audit Testing Procedure**: tasks, completion status, days, and comments\nAdd **Related Policies & Procedures** if applicable\nClick **Save** to create the engagement\nMost fields are mandatory — all marked fields must be completed\nYou can add more testing procedure rows using the **+ Add Task** button\nHistorical risks are read-only and shown for reference only\ncreate\nnew\nengagement\naudit\nplan\nadd\nschedule	{-0.01457977294921875,0.0285186767578125,0.053253173828125,-0.0501708984375,-0.057952880859375,-0.0201416015625,-0.007328033447265625,-0.0054168701171875,-0.003444671630859375,0.0074615478515625,0.049163818359375,-0.037750244140625,0.05712890625,-0.0299530029296875,0.020538330078125,-0.004055023193359375,-0.03704833984375,0.01340484619140625,-0.020263671875,0.0220794677734375,0.0292510986328125,0.043182373046875,0.0236663818359375,-0.0252227783203125,-0.0243988037109375,-0.040435791015625,-0.05438232421875,0.02001953125,-0.0182952880859375,-0.0225067138671875