cmn2wa1ry001vjc3o95dwoetd	audit-risk-assessment-config	internal-audit	Audit Settings	audit	{AuditHead}	How do I configure audit risk assessment scoring?	How do I configure audit risk assessment scoring?\nRisk assessment config\nScoring calculation setup\nRisk rating scales\nAudit risk levels\nConfigure risk assessment levels (Low, Medium, High) with numerical values, and set scoring calculation methods to standardize risk evaluations.\nNavigate to **Internal Audit** > **Audit Settings** > **Risk Assessment Configuration**\nIn **Audit Risk Assessment**: view/edit risk levels with labels and values (e.g., Low=5, Medium=7, High=10)\nClick **+ New Risk Assessment** to add a new level — enter Label and numeric Value\nUse **Edit** or **Delete** to modify existing levels\nIn **Scoring Calculation**: select the **Calculation Type** from dropdown (Product of all, Addition of all, High of all)\nDefine score ranges: Label, Lowest Value, Highest Value for each risk category\nClick **+ New Scoring Calculation** to add a new range\nClick **Save** to apply the configuration\nCalculation types: **Addition of all** (sums values), **High of all** (takes highest), **Product of all** (multiplies values)\nScore ranges determine how total scores map to risk categories (Low Risk, Medium Risk, High Risk)\nrisk\nassessment\nscoring\nconfiguration\ncalculation\nrating\nlevels	{-0.009674072265625,0.0198211669921875,0.08203125,-0.027740478515625,-0.036376953125,-0.0254058837890625,-0.0001240968704223633,-0.029327392578125,0.0090789794921875,0.007717132568359375,-0.0117340087890625,-0.05255126953125,-0.003124237060546875,-0.000545501708984375,0.060943603515625,-0.0244140625,0.003759384155273438,0.0208740234375,-0.0291290283203125,0.0235137939453125,0.01006317138671875,0.01537322998046875,0.022003173828125,-0.016937255859375,-0.00879669189453125,-0.0258026123046875,-0.01230621337890625,-0.033966064453125,-0.00144195556640625,0.003229141235351562,-0.001379013061523438,-0.028839111328125,0.0013151