cmn2wa21o0023jc3oj7cee47z	ca-org-context	organization	Context	grc	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I define internal and external context for my organization?	How do I define internal and external context for my organization?\nManage organization context factors\nAdd internal context\nAdd external context\nContext issues and actions\nOrganization risk context\nPreventive and corrective actions for context\nThe Organization Context page lets you define internal and external factors affecting risk and compliance posture, manage stakeholders, and track preventive/corrective actions for context issues.\nNavigate to **Organization** > **Context** from the sidebar\nDefine **internal context factors** — culture, governance, capabilities\nDefine **external context factors** — regulatory, market, technology\nManage **stakeholders** — add, edit, or delete stakeholders with type (Internal, External, Third Party) and status\nAssign **departments** to stakeholders and manage email/contact details\nAdd **document and file attachments** to context records\nTrack **issue actions** — both preventive and corrective actions\nUse **search** to find context records and **download** context data\nContext factors inform risk assessments and compliance planning across the GRC platform\nStakeholder management supports ISO 27001 and other framework requirements for interested parties\ncontext\ninternal\nexternal\nfactors\nstakeholders\nissues\npreventive\ncorrective\nactions	{-0.046112060546875,0.012786865234375,0.063720703125,0.03204345703125,-0.01090240478515625,-0.0245208740234375,0.0038604736328125,0.00969696044921875,-0.00859832763671875,0.0328369140625,0.0291748046875,-0.006877899169921875,0.0256805419921875,-0.04266357421875,0.0303955078125,-0.003370285034179688,0.0230560302734375,0.0200958251953125,-0.043060302734375,0.06280517578125,0.034454345703125,0.0333251953125,0.001317024230957031,0.06396484375,-0.0103912353515625,0.0106201171875,-0.0185089111328125,0.042999267578125,0.022506713