cmn2wa2220024jc3oi1nfoxjb	ca-org-users	organization	Users	grc	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I manage users as a Customer Administrator?	How do I manage users as a Customer Administrator?\nCreate user accounts\nAssign user roles and departments\nUser activation and blocking\nConfigure user language preferences\nTrack user login activity\nBulk user management\nAs Customer Administrator, you have full user management capabilities including creating users, assigning roles by function (Business, Security, Audit), setting departments, configuring preferences, and tracking login activity.\nNavigate to **Organization** > **Users** from the sidebar\nView all users with their role, department, status, and last login\nClick **Add New** to create a new user — enter username, email, first name, last name, designation, and function\nAssign a **role by function**: Business (Department Reviewer/Contributor), Security (Reviewer/Contributor), or Audit (AuditHead/AuditManager/Auditor/Auditee)\nSet the user's **department** and **reporting manager**\nConfigure **language preferences** and **timezone**\nUse **Activate** or **Block** actions to manage user access\nUse **Import** to bulk upload users via Excel — download the import template first\nUse **Export** to download the full user list\nUse **Search** and filters to find specific users\nAll mandatory fields must be completed before saving a new user\nFollow the import template structure strictly to avoid errors during bulk upload\nBlocked users cannot log in but their data is preserved\nLast login tracking helps monitor user activity\nusers\ncreate\nroles\ndepartments\nactivate\nblock\nlanguage\nlogin\nbulk\nimport\nexport	{-0.010711669921875,0.04534912109375,-0.005290985107421875,0.02325439453125,0.002431869506835938,-0.0286865234375,-0.0077667236328125,0.0236053466796875,0.03448486328125,0.055084228515625,0.00803375244140625,-0.030731201171875,0.0048370361328125,-0.0267791748046875,0.048431396484375,0.006683349609375,-0.03750610