cmn2wa22v0026jc3oprk2u5rm	ca-org-bia	organization	BIA	grc	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I configure and conduct Business Impact Analysis (BIA)?	How do I configure and conduct Business Impact Analysis (BIA)?\nBIA configuration and methodology\nSet RTO and RPO targets\nBIA categories setup\nBCP labels configuration\nBusiness continuity planning setup\nBIA impact ratings\nAs Customer Administrator, you can configure BIA categories, methodology, and BCP labels, as well as conduct BIA to identify critical processes and establish RTO/RPO targets.\nNavigate to **Organization** > **Settings** > **BIA** to configure BIA parameters\nConfigure **BIA Categories** — define assessment categories with sort order and active/inactive status\nConfigure **BIA Methodology** — set the BIA assessment approach for your organization\nConfigure **BCP Labels** — customize business continuity planning labels\nNavigate to **Organization** > **Process** > **Business Impact Analysis** to conduct BIA\nCreate BIA entries for business processes\nDefine **RTO** (Recovery Time Objective) — maximum acceptable time to restore a process\nDefine **RPO** (Recovery Point Objective) — maximum acceptable data loss measured in time\nSet **impact ratings** across categories: financial, operational, reputational, legal\nDetermine **process criticality** based on the impact analysis results\nBIA results drive business continuity planning and risk prioritization\nThe highest impact score across all activities is used as the overall rating\nThe Performance Dashboard provides visual KPIs following BIA analysis\nbia\nbusiness impact\nrto\nrpo\ncategories\nmethodology\nbcp\ncontinuity\nimpact\nratings\nrecovery	{-0.036285400390625,0.05181884765625,0.075439453125,0.0091400146484375,-0.03619384765625,-0.05859375,-0.01134490966796875,2.419948577880859e-05,0.005397796630859375,0.0124359130859375,0.01245880126953125,0.0089569091796875,-0.002145767211914062,-0.068115234375,0.02410888671875,0.038787841796875,-0.01983642578