cmn2wa2lz002mjc3oqcjeqkec	ca-risk-settings	risk-management	Settings	grc	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I configure risk management settings as Customer Administrator?	How do I configure risk management settings as Customer Administrator?\nRisk category management\nRisk type definitions\nRisk rating matrix customization\nThreshold configuration for risks\nRisk methodology setup\nControl strength and vulnerability settings\nConfigure all risk management parameters including categories, types, rating matrix, thresholds, control strength, likelihood, threats, vulnerabilities, methodology, and impact definitions.\nNavigate to **Risk Management** > **Settings** from the sidebar\nConfigure **Risk Category** — manage categories (Cyber, Operations, Legal, Physical, Cloud) with active/inactive status\nConfigure **Risk Type** — define risk type classifications\nConfigure **Control Strength** — define levels to evaluate control effectiveness with name and score\nConfigure **Likelihood** — set probability measurement and scoring scales\nConfigure **Threat** — manage predefined threats\nConfigure **Vulnerability** — manage predefined vulnerabilities\nConfigure **Risk Methodology** — set the formula: Risk Score = Likelihood x Impact x Asset Score x Vulnerability Score\nConfigure **Impact** — define impact categories and severity levels with name, score, and description\nConfigure **Vulnerability Rating** — define severity levels and corresponding scores\nConfigure **Threshold** — set risk acceptance thresholds\nOnly Customer Administrators and GRC Administrators can access risk settings\nRisk methodology defines how risk scores are calculated across the platform\nChanges affect all risk assessments within your tenant\nsettings\nrisk\ncategory\ntype\nrating\nthreshold\nmethodology\ncontrol strength\nvulnerability\nthreat	{-0.02923583984375,0.03448486328125,0.0640869140625,0.01263427734375,-0.042236328125,-0.04266357421875,-0.003252029418945312,0.013946533203125,0.0174407958984375,0