cmn2wa2n6002pjc3oljlwxdce	ca-asset-classification	asset-management	Classification	grc	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I classify assets as Customer Administrator?	How do I classify assets as Customer Administrator?\nCIA classification for assets\nAsset confidentiality integrity availability\nClassification hierarchy management\nDefine classification levels\nAsset handling and protection requirements\nAsset grouping and organization\nClassify assets based on confidentiality, integrity, and availability (CIA) requirements using a hierarchical classification system with Category, Sub-Category, and Group levels.\nNavigate to **Asset Management** > **Classification** from the sidebar\nView existing classifications with search and export options\nClick **New Asset Classification** to create a new entry\nSet the **classification hierarchy**: Category > Sub-Category > Group\nDefine **classification levels**: Public, Internal, Confidential, Restricted\nClassify assets by **CIA impact**:\nRate **Confidentiality** — protection from unauthorized access\nRate **Integrity** — data accuracy and protection from unauthorized modification\nRate **Availability** — importance of being accessible without downtime\nSet **handling and protection requirements** per classification\nThe **Asset Criticality Score** is calculated automatically\nClick **Save** to create the classification\nUse the Action column to edit or delete existing classifications\nThe CIA model is the industry standard for information security classification\nclassification\ncia\nconfidentiality\nintegrity\navailability\nhierarchy\nlevels\nhandling\nprotection\ngrouping	{-0.030303955078125,0.01580810546875,0.05096435546875,0.012786865234375,-0.009124755859375,-0.007366180419921875,-0.011993408203125,-0.028656005859375,0.002580642700195312,-0.002191543579101562,0.0211181640625,-0.031341552734375,0.003955841064453125,-0.018890380859375,-0.02130126953125,-0.02996826171875,0.004261016845703125,0.030059814453125,-0.04409790039