cmn2wa2nk002qjc3o9yywlds7	ca-asset-settings	asset-management	Settings	grc	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I configure asset management settings as Customer Administrator?	How do I configure asset management settings as Customer Administrator?\nAsset type configuration\nClassification level definitions\nCIA scoring configuration\nAsset category and sub-category setup\nAsset sensitivity and lifecycle settings\nAsset master data setup\nConfigure asset management parameters including asset types, categories, sub-categories, groups, sensitivity levels, lifecycle statuses, and CIA scoring methods.\nNavigate to **Asset Management** > **Settings** from the sidebar\nConfigure **Asset Category** — define broad classifications (IT, Facilities, Finance) with title and status\nConfigure **Asset Sub-Category** — add with title, asset category, and status (Active/Inactive)\nConfigure **Asset Group** — add with name, description, status, and linked sub-categories\nConfigure **Asset Sensitivity** — define sensitivity levels (Confidential, Internal, Public)\nConfigure **Asset Lifecycle** — define lifecycle stages for assets (Active, Retired, etc.)\nConfigure **CIA Scoring**:\nDefine **Confidentiality** levels (C1, C2, etc.) with labels and values\nDefine **Integrity** levels (I1, I2, etc.) with labels and values\nDefine **Availability** levels (A1, A2, etc.) with labels and values\nSet **Scoring Calculation** method: High of all, Addition of all, or Product of all\nDefine **Ranges** (High/Low) to categorize total scores into risk levels\nOnly Customer Administrators and GRC Administrators can access asset settings\nChanges to CIA scoring affect how asset criticality is calculated\nsettings\nasset\ntype\nclassification\ncia\nscoring\ncategory\nsubcategory\nsensitivity\nlifecycle	{-0.0201263427734375,0.026031494140625,0.06768798828125,-0.003797531127929688,-0.02838134765625,-0.025360107421875,0.010040283203125,-0.0224151611328125,0.00557708740234375,0.01439666748046875,0.011161804199218