cmn2wa2wm002wjc3ogpf9dywe	ca-audit-planning	internal-audit	Audit Planning	audit	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I create and manage audit plans as Customer Administrator?	How do I create and manage audit plans as Customer Administrator?\nCreate audit engagements\nAnnual audit plan management\nAssign auditors to engagements\nLink risks to audit plans\nAudit testing procedures\nGenerate annual plan report\nCreate and manage audit engagements with defined scope, objectives, timelines, team assignments, and risk linkages. Generate annual audit plan reports for management review.\nNavigate to **Internal Audit** > **Audit Planning** from the sidebar\nView all engagements with: Audit ID, Title, Department, Type, Auditor, Status\nClick **Add Engagement** to create a new audit engagement\nFill in: **Engagement Title**, **Objective**, **Scope** (mandatory fields)\nSelect the **Department** being audited\n**Link Open Risks** in the selected department to the engagement\nReview **Historical Risks** from previous years for reference\nSelect **Audit Rating** (High, Medium, Low) and **Audit Type** (Regular, Follow-up, Special)\nAssign the **Auditor** and **Auditee**\nSet **Start Date** and **Target Date**\nUpload **Attachments** and **Workpapers**\nFill in the **Audit Testing Procedure**: tasks, completion status, days, and comments\nAdd **Related Policies & Procedures** if applicable\nClick **Save** to create the engagement\nClick **Generate Annual Plan Report** for a summarized annual report (PDF downloadable)\nUse filters by **Department** and **Status** to narrow the list\nMost fields are mandatory and must be completed before saving\nUse **+ Add Task** to add additional testing procedure rows\nHistorical risks are read-only and shown for reference only\nUse **Export** to download the audit plan list in Excel format\naudit\nplanning\nengagements\nannual\nplan\nassign\nauditors\nrisks\ntesting\nreport	{-0.029937744140625,0.0285491943359375,0.0653076171875,-0.037750244140625,-0.0