cmn2wa3540032jc3odx146qb3	ca-audit-settings	internal-audit	Audit Settings	audit	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I configure audit settings as Customer Administrator?	How do I configure audit settings as Customer Administrator?\nAudit types configuration\nAudit department management\nAudit periodicity settings\nRisk assessment matrix for audit\nAudit categories and control nature\nAudit escalation policies\nAudit user management\nConfigure the internal audit function including audit types, departments, periodicity, processes, risk assessment matrices, categories, control nature, user management, and escalation policies.\nNavigate to **Internal Audit** > **Settings** from the sidebar\nConfigure **Audit Types** — define types such as Internal, External, Compliance, Operational\nConfigure **Departments** — manage departments for audit scope\nConfigure **Periodicity** — set audit frequency/cycle (Monthly, Quarterly, Annually)\nConfigure **Process** — define processes and sub-processes for audit scope\nConfigure **Risk Assessment** — set probability/impact matrices, risk levels, and scoring calculations\nConfigure **Categories** — define audit categories\nConfigure **Nature of Controls** — define control types (Preventive, Detective, Corrective)\nConfigure **User Management** — manage audit team members, add accounts, assign roles (Audit Head, Audit Manager, Auditor, Auditee)\nConfigure **Escalation** — set reminder rules and days for overdue events (Response Submission, Acknowledgement, Clarification, Interview, Issue Resolution)\nAudit settings configuration requires Customer Administrator or Audit Head role\nChanges to settings affect all audit operations within your tenant\nEscalation rules send automatic reminders for overdue audit events\naudit\nsettings\ntypes\ndepartments\nperiodicity\nrisk assessment\ncategories\ncontrols\nescalation\nuser management	{-0.041259765625,0.024200439453125,0.06951904296875,-0.0282440185546875,-0.05230712890625,-0.00604248046875,0.01107