cmn2wa35j0033jc3o63u73r2u	dr-role-overview	general	Roles & Permissions	grc	{DepartmentReviewer}	What can I do as a Department Reviewer?	What can I do as a Department Reviewer?\nDepartment Reviewer capabilities\nWhat is the Department Reviewer role\nDepartment Reviewer permissions\nWhat modules can I access as Department Reviewer\nDepartment Reviewer role overview\nWhat does a Department Reviewer do\nDepartment-scoped reviewer access\nAs a Department Reviewer, you are a reviewer scoped to your assigned department. You can view and review data only within your department's scope across Organization, Compliance, Risk Management, and Asset Management modules. You do not have access to Internal Audit.\nYou have **department-scoped view** access to **Organization** — profile, context, users, processes, BIA, and settings (you will only see data within your assigned department)\nYou have **department-scoped view and review** access to **Compliance** — frameworks, controls, governance, evidence, exceptions, KPIs, risk matrix, reports, and master data\nYou have **department-scoped view and review** access to **Risk Management** — dashboard, register, assessment, response, risk control matrix, settings, and reports\nYou have **department-scoped view and review** access to **Asset Management** — inventory, classification, settings, and reports\nYou can **approve or reject** department-scoped items such as risks, controls, evidence, and governance documents\nYour access is limited to data within your assigned department only\nYou do NOT have access to Internal Audit modules\nYou cannot create, edit, or delete records — your role is focused on reviewing and approving\nData from other departments will not be visible to you\nIf you need broader access, contact your Customer Administrator to adjust your role\ndepartment\nreviewer\nrole\ncapabilities\npermissions\nmodules\naccess\nscope\nreview\napprove	{-0.024139404296875,0.05657958984375,0.033477783203125,0.051239013671875,-0.01892