cmn2wa3uy003ujc3oyg4ad08y	ga-role-overview	general	Roles & Permissions	both	{GRCAdministrator}	What can I do as a GRC Administrator?	What can I do as a GRC Administrator?\nGRC Administrator capabilities\nWhat is my role as GRC Admin\nGRC Admin permissions\nWhat modules can I access as GRC Administrator\nGRC Admin role overview\nWhat does GRC Administrator do\nSuperadmin access and capabilities\nSystem administrator role\nAs a GRC Administrator, you are the system-level superadmin with unrestricted access to ALL modules across ALL tenants. You manage customer accounts, system-wide settings, compliance master data, and have full CRUD access to every module in every organization.\nYou have exclusive access to **GRC Administration** — customer accounts, compliance master data, email settings, and system configuration\nYou have full access to **Organization** — profile, context, users, processes, BIA, and settings across all tenants\nYou have full access to **Compliance** — frameworks, controls, governance, evidence, exceptions, KPIs, risk matrix, reports, and master data across all tenants\nYou have full access to **Risk Management** — dashboard, register, assessment, response, risk control matrix, settings, and reports across all tenants\nYou have full access to **Asset Management** — inventory, classification, settings, and reports across all tenants\nYou have full access to **Internal Audit** — dashboard, universe, risk identification, planning, fieldwork, findings, CAPA, reports, document library, and settings across all tenants\nYou have system-wide visibility across all departments and all customer tenants\nYou can create, activate, block, and delete customer accounts\nYou can configure system-wide settings including SSO, email, import/export, and PDF reports\nYou can manage compliance master data (frameworks, controls, templates) that apply system-wide\nUnlike Customer Administrators, your access is not limited to a single tenant\ngrc\nadministrator\nsuperadmin\n