cmn2wa3vi003vjc3o0pqwndhk	ga-admin-customer-accounts	grc-admin	Customer Accounts	grc	{GRCAdministrator}	How do I manage customer accounts as a GRC Administrator?	How do I manage customer accounts as a GRC Administrator?\nCreate a new customer account\nEdit customer account details\nDelete a customer account\nActivate or block a customer\nManage tenant organizations\nSet subscription module flags for a customer\nUpload customer logo\nConfigure customer language and timezone\nThe Customer Accounts page provides multi-tenant customer management. As a GRC Administrator, you can create, edit, delete, activate, and block customer organizations, configure their subscription modules, and manage their branding and settings.\nNavigate to **GRC Administration** > **Customer Accounts** from the sidebar (Sidebar → GRC → Customer Accounts)\nView the **list of all customer accounts** with their status, contact details, and subscription flags\nClick **Create** to add a new customer account — enter organization name, contact email, phone, and address\nSet **subscription module flags**: isGrcAdded, isTprmAdded, isQpostComplianceEnabled to control which modules the customer can access\nUpload a **customer logo** for branding purposes\nConfigure **language** and **timezone** settings for the customer\nAssign a **primary contact** email for the customer account\nUse the **Activate/Block** toggle to enable or disable customer access to the system\nClick **Delete** to permanently remove a customer account (use with caution)\nOnly GRC Administrators have access to customer account management — this page is not visible to any other role\nBlocking a customer account prevents all users in that tenant from logging in\nDeleting a customer account is irreversible — ensure all data has been backed up if needed\nSubscription module flags control which product modules (GRC, TPRM, QPOST) are available to the customer\nChanges to customer settings take effect immediately across that tenant\ncustomer\