cmn2wa40i003xjc3of93x5sfp	ga-admin-email-settings	grc-admin	Email Settings	grc	{GRCAdministrator}	How do I configure email and SMTP settings?	How do I configure email and SMTP settings?\nSet up SMTP for notifications\nConfigure email server settings\nManage email templates\nSet notification email addresses\nEmail configuration for the system\nHow to enable email notifications\nThe Email Settings page allows GRC Administrators to configure SMTP server settings, manage email templates, and set up notification email addresses for system-wide alerts and reminders.\nNavigate to **GRC Administration** > **Email Settings** from the sidebar (Sidebar → GRC → Email Settings)\nConfigure **SMTP settings** — enter the mail server host, port, authentication credentials, and encryption type (TLS/SSL)\nSet the **sender email address** and **display name** for outgoing system emails\nManage **email templates** — customize the content and formatting of notification emails\nConfigure **notification email settings** — define which events trigger email notifications (due date reminders, approval requests, etc.)\nTest the email configuration by sending a **test email** to verify SMTP connectivity\nOnly GRC Administrators can configure email settings — this affects notifications system-wide\nSMTP credentials are stored securely and are not visible after saving\nEmail notifications include due date reminders for evidence, CAPA/findings, and policy reviews\nIncorrect SMTP settings will prevent all system email notifications from being sent\nEnsure the sender email address is authorized by your mail server to avoid delivery issues\nemail\nsmtp\nsettings\nnotifications\ntemplates\nserver\nconfiguration\nmail\nalerts	{-0.0057220458984375,0.03680419921875,0.0550537109375,-0.037841796875,-0.017852783203125,-0.01422882080078125,0.0199432373046875,-0.017120361328125,0.0234832763671875,0.01441192626953125,-0.0183563232421875,0.032562255859375,0.002288818359375,-0.0005106925964355469,0.0246734619140