cmn2wa41b003zjc3ohmqw59mb	dc-role-overview	general	Roles & Permissions	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	What can I do as a Department Contributor?	What can I do as a Department Contributor?\nWhat is the Department Contributor role?\nWhat are my permissions as Department Contributor?\nWhat modules can a Department Contributor access?\nDepartment Contributor capabilities\nWhat is the difference between Department Contributor and Department Reviewer?\nCan I create records as Department Contributor?\nWhat pages can I see as Department Contributor?\nThe Department Contributor role is scoped to your assigned department. Unlike the Department Reviewer (view-only), you can actively create and edit records within Compliance, Risk Management, and Asset Management for your department.\nYou have access to three modules: **Compliance**, **Risk Management**, and **Asset Management** — all scoped to your department\nYou can **create and edit** risks within your department's scope\nYou can **submit evidence** for controls assigned to your department\nYou can **update asset information** for assets belonging to your department\nYou can **create compliance exception requests** for your department\nYou can **view** department-scoped data across all three modules including dashboards, reports, and matrices\nYou do **NOT** have access to Organization settings, Internal Audit, TPRM, or GRC Administration modules\nYour access is limited to records within your assigned department — you cannot view or modify records belonging to other departments\nUnlike the Department Reviewer role which is view-only, your role allows you to create and edit records\nYou cannot delete records or approve/reject submissions — those actions require higher-level roles\nIf a sidebar menu item or action button is not visible, your role does not have the required permission\ndepartment contributor\nrole\npermissions\nscope\ndepartment\ncreate\nedit\ncapabilities	{0.021453857421875,0.0299224853515625,0.0340576171875,0.0