cmn2wa4240041jc3o45pki7he	dc-comp-controls	compliance	Control Assessment	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I work with compliance controls as a Department Contributor?	How do I work with compliance controls as a Department Contributor?\nHow to assess controls in my department?\nHow to view control status?\nCan I edit controls as Department Contributor?\nHow to link controls to evidence?\nHow to filter controls by framework?\nWhere do I see control assessment status?\nHow to map controls to risks?\nView and contribute to compliance control assessments for your department. You can assess control effectiveness, link controls to evidence, and map controls to risks — all within your department's scope.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Controls**\nView the list of controls with status indicators (Compliant, Partially Compliant, Non-Compliant, Not Assessed)\nUse filters to narrow by **framework**, **domain**, or **status**\nClick on a control to view its details including code, name, description, domain, and category\n**Assess control effectiveness** — update the assessment status for controls in your department\n**Link controls to evidence** items to demonstrate compliance\n**Map controls to risks** to show risk coverage\nUse multi-select column filtering and search to find specific controls\nYou can create and edit controls within your department's scope — this distinguishes you from the Department Reviewer who can only view\nControls outside your department will not be visible or editable\nBulk assessment capabilities are available for efficient processing\nPagination is available for navigating large control sets\ncontrol\nassessment\ncompliance\ncompliant\nnon-compliant\nevidence\ndepartment\nedit	{0.01849365234375,0.0296630859375,0.04632568359375,0.0151214599609375,-0.017333984375,-0.0118865966796875,-0.00804901123046875,0.01049041748046875,0.022979736328125,0.07684326171875,0.050689697265625,-0.00977325439453125,0.045379638671875,0.0004057884216308594,0.034240