cmn2wa42m0042jc3oaztst3ja	dc-comp-governance	compliance	Governance Documents	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I manage governance documents as a Department Contributor?	How do I manage governance documents as a Department Contributor?\nHow to create a policy document?\nHow to upload governance documents?\nCan I edit governance documents in my department?\nHow to create a procedure or standard?\nWhere do I manage policies?\nHow to attach files to a governance document?\nHow to link documents to frameworks?\nCreate and edit governance documents (policies, procedures, standards, guidelines) within your department's scope. You can upload files, link documents to frameworks and controls, and track version history.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Governance**\nView the list of governance documents with version and status information\nClick **Create** to add a new document — select the document type (policy, procedure, standard, guideline)\nFill in document properties: code, name, version, and document type\n**Edit document content and metadata** as needed for your department's documents\n**Upload supporting files/attachments** to the document\n**Link the document to frameworks and controls** for traceability\nSet review schedules, due dates, and assign owners/reviewers\nTrack **version history** to see how the document has evolved\nAs a Department Contributor you can create and edit documents scoped to your department — the Department Reviewer role can only view\nDocument review and approval workflows may require higher-level roles for final approval\nYou can download documents for offline review\nEvidence can be attached to governance documents to support compliance\ngovernance\npolicy\nprocedure\nstandard\nguideline\ndocument\nupload\ncreate\nedit\nversion	{0.021453857421875,0.048797607421875,0.0574951171875,0.003978729248046875,0.00682830810546875,-0.0111846923828125,-0.020538330078125,0.004894256591796875,0.005542755126953125,0.05078125,0.040679931640625,-0.00