cmn2wa4300043jc3o0csnr6wy	dc-comp-evidence	compliance	Evidence Management	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I submit evidence as a Department Contributor?	How do I submit evidence as a Department Contributor?\nHow to upload evidence?\nHow to respond to an evidence request?\nHow to link evidence to controls?\nWhere do I manage evidence for my department?\nHow to submit evidence for compliance?\nCan I create evidence items?\nHow to check evidence status?\nHow to attach files as evidence?\nSubmit and manage evidence items for your department's controls. Upload files, link evidence to specific controls and frameworks, and track submission status (Pending, Submitted, Approved, Rejected).\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Evidence**\nView evidence items assigned to your department with their status and due dates\nClick **Create** to submit a new evidence item for a department control\n**Upload evidence files** — documents, screenshots, exports, or other supporting materials\n**Link the evidence to specific controls** and frameworks to demonstrate compliance\nSet the evidence collection **due date** if applicable\nSubmit the evidence for review — status will change from Pending to Submitted\nTrack the status of your submissions: **Pending**, **Submitted**, **Approved**, or **Rejected**\nIf evidence is rejected, review the feedback, update the submission, and resubmit\nAs a Department Contributor you can create and submit evidence — this is a key responsibility distinguishing you from view-only roles\nEvidence is scoped to your department — you can only submit evidence for controls assigned to your department\nAI-powered evidence suggestions may help identify what evidence to provide\nEvidence versioning allows you to update submissions while preserving history\nUse filters to find evidence by status, assignee, or control\nevidence\nsubmit\nupload\ncompliance\ncontrol\nfile\npending\napproved\nrejected\ndepartment	{0.0229034423828125,0.00780487060546875,0.0354614257812