cmn2wa43f0044jc3o7yxhc2ye	dc-comp-exceptions	compliance	Exceptions	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I create a compliance exception request as a Department Contributor?	How do I create a compliance exception request as a Department Contributor?\nHow to request a compliance exception?\nHow to document a control exception?\nWhere do I manage exceptions for my department?\nCan I create exception requests?\nHow to specify compensating controls for an exception?\nHow to track exception approval status?\nWhat is a compliance exception?\nCreate and manage compliance exception requests for your department. Exceptions document situations where a control cannot be fully implemented, requiring risk acceptance or compensating controls.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Exceptions**\nView the list of compliance exceptions with status indicators for your department\nClick **Create** to submit a new exception request\nFill in exception properties: code, description, and severity level\nProvide a **justification** explaining why the control cannot be fully implemented\nSpecify any **compensating controls** that mitigate the risk\nSet the **expiry/target remediation date** for the exception\nAssign the department and owner for the exception\n**Link the exception to the relevant control(s)**\nSubmit the request — track approval status (Open, In-Progress, Closed)\nAs a Department Contributor you can create and edit exception requests within your department — a key capability not available to view-only roles\nException approval typically requires a higher-level role (manager or administrator)\nVisual indicators (pie chart, status timeline) help you track exception status across your department\nYou can edit exceptions to update justifications or compensating controls before approval\nexception\ncompliance\ncompensating control\nrisk acceptance\nwaiver\nexemption\ndepartment\ncreate	{0.0108489990234375,0.033233642578125,0.03338623046875,0.01406097412109375,-0.013427734375,-0.01060