cmn2wa4bi004bjc3oipgyg67a	dc-risk-assessment	risk-management	Risk Assessment	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I perform a risk assessment as a Department Contributor?	How do I perform a risk assessment as a Department Contributor?\nHow to assess risk likelihood and impact?\nHow to use the risk assessment matrix?\nHow to do inherent vs residual risk assessment?\nHow to use the assessment wizard?\nWhere do I assess risks for my department?\nHow to document assessment rationale?\nHow to view the risk heatmap?\nPerform detailed risk assessments for your department using likelihood and impact matrices. Use the structured assessment wizard to evaluate risks quantitatively and qualitatively, comparing inherent vs. residual risk levels.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Risk Management → Risk Assessment**\nView the risk assessment matrix (5×5 likelihood vs. impact) for your department\nSelect a risk to assess — click on it to open the assessment form\nUse the **assessment wizard** for structured step-by-step input\nPerform **inherent risk assessment** — evaluate the risk before any controls are applied\nPerform **residual risk assessment** — evaluate the risk after controls are applied\n**Document assessment rationale** explaining your scoring decisions\nMap relevant **threats and vulnerabilities** to the risk\nReview the **risk heatmap** visualization to see the overall risk landscape\nSet the assessment status: Draft, Submitted, Approved, Rejected, or In-Progress\nCompare **inherent vs. residual risk levels** to gauge control effectiveness\nAs a Department Contributor you can create and edit risk assessments — not just view them\nAssessments are scoped to your department's risks only\nThe 5×5 matrix helps standardize risk evaluation across the organization\nAssessment criteria and scales are defined by your organization's risk framework\nDraft assessments can be saved and completed later\nrisk assessment\nlikelihood\nimpact\nmatrix\nheatmap\ninherent\nresidual\nwizard\ndepartmen