cmn2wa4c2004cjc3oz8lua7gf	dc-risk-response	risk-management	Risk Response	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I create risk response plans as a Department Contributor?	How do I create risk response plans as a Department Contributor?\nHow to define a risk treatment plan?\nHow to set a risk mitigation strategy?\nHow to create action plans for risks?\nHow to track risk response progress?\nWhere do I manage risk treatments?\nHow to assign action owners for risk response?\nWhat risk strategies can I choose?\nPlan and track risk treatment actions for your department's risks. Define response strategies (Mitigate, Accept, Transfer, Avoid), create action plans, assign owners, and monitor implementation progress.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Risk Management → Risk Response**\nView risks in your department that require response or treatment\nSelect a risk and define the **response strategy**: Mitigate, Accept, Transfer, or Avoid\n**Create treatment action plans** with specific activities and due dates\n**Assign action owners** responsible for implementing each action\nSet **due dates** for each action item\nTrack **action implementation status**: Open, In-Progress, or Completed\nMonitor **response progress** to ensure treatments are on track\n**Document response effectiveness** after implementation\nAs a Department Contributor you can create and edit risk response plans — a key capability for actively managing your department's risks\nRisk response is scoped to your department — you only see and manage responses for your department's risks\nEach risk can have multiple action items with different owners and due dates\nResponse progress tracking helps ensure timely completion of treatment plans\nrisk response\ntreatment\nmitigation\nstrategy\naction plan\nmitigate\naccept\ntransfer\navoid	{-0.0189666748046875,0.02227783203125,0.06036376953125,0.01433563232421875,-0.034271240234375,-0.0606689453125,-0.0144500732421875,0.022674560546875,0.017059326171875,0.036041259765625,0.023330688476