cmn2wa4ch004djc3onn292x3x	dc-risk-control-matrix	risk-management	Risk Control Matrix	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I use the Risk Control Matrix as a Department Contributor?	How do I use the Risk Control Matrix as a Department Contributor?\nHow to view risk-control mappings?\nHow to link controls to risks?\nHow to identify risk coverage gaps?\nWhere is the risk control matrix?\nHow to see which controls address which risks?\nHow to check residual risk after controls?\nView and manage the Risk Control Matrix for your department. Map relationships between risks and controls, identify coverage gaps, and review residual risk calculations.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Risk Management → Risk Control Matrix**\nView the matrix showing **risks vs. controls** for your department\nReview status indicators for each control-risk link\n**Link controls to risks** to document mitigation relationships\n**Unlink controls** from risks if a relationship no longer applies\nIdentify **unmitigated risks** — risks without linked controls representing coverage gaps\nReview **control effectiveness** per risk\nCheck **residual risk calculations** showing remaining risk after controls\nUse **collapsible risk groups** to organize the view\nSearch and filter to find specific risk-control relationships\nAs a Department Contributor you can link and unlink controls to risks — not just view the matrix\nThe matrix is scoped to your department's risks and controls\nUnmitigated risks (gaps) should be addressed by creating new controls or adjusting risk response plans\nResidual risk calculation helps quantify the effectiveness of your department's control environment\nrisk control matrix\nmapping\ncontrol\nrisk\ngap\ncoverage\nresidual\nlink	{-0.01508331298828125,0.06134033203125,0.029815673828125,0.027618408203125,-0.02947998046875,-0.019622802734375,0.0002204179763793945,0.0006928443908691406,0.0087127685546875,0.0487060546875,0.0008635520935058594,-0.027679443359375,0.011871337890625,-0.007099151611