cmn2wa4j7004hjc3ot6yv1g7w	dc-asset-classification	asset-management	Asset Classification	grc	{DepartmentContributor}	How do I classify assets as a Department Contributor?	How do I classify assets as a Department Contributor?\nHow to set asset classification?\nHow to assign CIA ratings to assets?\nHow to use confidentiality integrity availability classification?\nWhere do I classify department assets?\nWhat are the classification levels?\nHow to set handling requirements for assets?\nHow to view the classification hierarchy?\nClassify assets in your department based on Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability (CIA) requirements. Set classification levels and handling/protection requirements using the hierarchical classification system.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Asset Management → Classification**\nView the **classification hierarchy**: Category → Sub-Category → Group\nBrowse existing classification definitions and levels\n**Classify assets** by setting their CIA impact levels (Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability)\nDefine **classification levels**: Public, Internal, Confidential, or Restricted\nSet **handling and protection requirements** appropriate to each classification level\nOrganize assets into proper **groups** within the hierarchy\nCreate or edit classification entries for your department's assets\nAs a Department Contributor you can create and edit classifications for your department's assets — not just view them\nThe classification hierarchy (Category → Sub-Category → Group) provides structured organization\nCIA ratings directly affect the security controls required for each asset\nProper classification is essential for compliance with data protection requirements\nasset classification\nCIA\nconfidentiality\nintegrity\navailability\npublic\ninternal\nconfidential\nrestricted	{-0.01088714599609375,0.01192474365234375,0.072998046875,0.00852203369140625,0.01194000244140625,0.00909423828125,-0.001739501953125,-0.0178375244140625,0.01251220703125,0.0098876