cmn2wa4kg004kjc3oot0bxjnw	rv-role-overview	general	Roles & Permissions	both	{Reviewer}	What can a Reviewer do in the GRC application?	What can a Reviewer do in the GRC application?\nWhat is the Reviewer role?\nWhat permissions does a Reviewer have?\nWhat modules can a Reviewer access?\nReviewer capabilities overview\nWhat is the difference between Reviewer and DepartmentReviewer?\nCan a Reviewer see all departments?\nReviewer role summary\nThe Reviewer is a cross-module role with organization-wide visibility. You can view data across all departments and modules, review and comment on risks, controls, and findings, approve or reject evidence and governance documents, and access all dashboards and reports. Unlike the DepartmentReviewer (limited to one department), you have full cross-department visibility.\n**Organization** — View organization profile, context, users, business processes, BIA, and settings (read-only)\n**Compliance** — View frameworks, controls, governance documents, evidence, exceptions, KPIs, risk matrix, reports, and master data. Approve/reject evidence and review governance documents\n**Risk Management** — View risk dashboard, risk register, risk assessment, risk response, risk control matrix, settings, and reports (read-only)\n**Asset Management** — View asset inventory, classification, settings, and reports (read-only)\n**Internal Audit** — View audit dashboard, universe, risk identification, risk register, planning, fieldwork, findings, CAPA tracking, reports, document library, and settings (read-only)\nReviewer has organization-wide visibility — you see data from ALL departments, not just your own\nThis role is different from DepartmentReviewer, which is scoped to a single department\nUnlike CustomerAdministrator, you cannot create, edit, or delete most records — your focus is review and approval\nYour primary value is cross-department oversight, ensuring consistency and quality across the organization\nIf you need to create or modify records, 