cmn2wa5o7005ljc3oi60c35ff	rv-audit-settings	internal-audit	Audit Settings	audit	{Reviewer}	How do I view audit settings and configuration?	How do I view audit settings and configuration?\nWhere are audit types configured?\nHow to see audit department setup?\nAudit settings for Reviewer\nWhere to view escalation policies?\nHow to check audit periodicity?\nWhere to see risk assessment matrices for audit?\nView audit function configuration including audit types, departments, periodicity, processes, risk assessment matrices, categories, control nature, user management, and escalation policies. As a Reviewer you have read-only access.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Settings**\nReview **Audit Types** — internal, external, compliance, operational definitions\nReview **Departments** — department management configuration\nCheck **Periodicity** — audit frequency and cycle settings\nReview **Process** — process and sub-process definitions for audit scope\nCheck **Risk Assessment** — probability and impact matrices\nReview **Categories** — audit category definitions\nCheck **Nature of Controls** — control types and characteristics\nReview **User Management** — audit team member assignments and roles\nCheck **Escalation** policies for audit findings\nSettings are managed by the Audit Head — you have view-only access\nUnderstanding audit configuration helps contextualize audit results you review\nEscalation policies are important to understand when reviewing overdue findings and CAPAs\naudit settings\naudit types\ndepartments\nperiodicity\nescalation\nrisk assessment\ncategories	{-0.046875,0.031829833984375,0.0675048828125,-0.017669677734375,-0.047515869140625,0.0174713134765625,0.007709503173828125,-0.01555633544921875,0.03179931640625,0.007801055908203125,0.019805908203125,-0.053863525390625,0.041961669921875,0.01312255859375,0.0355224609375,0.004993438720703125,-0.01499176025390625,0.031097412109375,-0.003072738647460938,0.07049560546875,0.0743408203125,0.0291900634