cmn2wa5ra005sjc3owuexhezb	aud-audit-fieldwork	internal-audit	Fieldwork	audit	{Auditor}	How do I conduct fieldwork as an Auditor?	How do I conduct fieldwork as an Auditor?\nHow to perform audit fieldwork?\nWhere do I execute my audit tasks?\nHow to create work papers?\nHow to upload audit evidence?\nHow to document observations during an audit?\nWhere do I record interview notes?\nHow to track fieldwork completion?\nHow to add findings from fieldwork?\nThe Fieldwork page is your primary workspace. Here you conduct testing, gather evidence, create work papers, document observations, record interview notes, and create draft findings for your assigned engagements.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Fieldwork**\nReview the list of engagements showing **title, department, status, dates, and assigned auditor**\nClick on an engagement assigned to you to open its fieldwork details\n**Create work papers** to document your testing procedures and results\n**Upload audit evidence** and supporting files (documents, screenshots, exports)\n**Record interview notes** from discussions with auditees and process owners\n**Document observations** as you identify issues during testing\n**Create draft findings** when you discover gaps or non-conformities\nTrack your **fieldwork completion status** as you progress through tasks\nUse **filters** (department, status, auditor) to find specific engagements\nFieldwork is your primary function as an Auditor — this is where you spend most of your time\nAlways link evidence and work papers to the correct engagement\nDraft findings created here will be reviewed and finalized by the Audit Head or Manager\nEnsure observations are clearly documented with supporting evidence\nInterview notes should capture key points, attendees, and dates\nYou can view compliance controls and evidence from the Compliance module to support your testing\nfieldwork\nwork papers\nobservations\nevidence\ninterview notes\ntesting\naudit tasks	{-0.002689361572265625,0.