cmn2wa5rp005tjc3ojns2n13h	aud-audit-findings	internal-audit	Findings	audit	{Auditor}	How do I create and manage findings as an Auditor?	How do I create and manage findings as an Auditor?\nHow to create audit findings?\nHow do I document a finding?\nHow to classify finding severity?\nWhere to track finding status?\nHow to add recommendations to findings?\nHow to link findings to controls and risks?\nWhat severity levels are available for findings?\nCreate and manage audit findings discovered during fieldwork. Findings document gaps between current state and expected criteria, classified by severity with recommendations for remediation.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Fieldwork**, then access findings from within an engagement\nClick **Create Finding** (or equivalent action) to add a new finding\nEnter the **finding title** and a detailed **description** of the issue\nSelect a **severity level**: Critical, High, Medium, Low, or Informational\nAdd your **recommendation** for how to remediate the finding\n**Assign a finding owner** responsible for remediation\nSet a **remediation due date**\n**Link the finding to relevant controls and risks** if applicable\nReview and save the finding as a **draft** for Audit Head/Manager review\nFindings are created as drafts — the Audit Head or Manager will review and finalize them\nAlways include clear, specific descriptions with supporting evidence references\nSeverity classification drives prioritization: Critical and High findings require urgent attention\nLinking findings to controls helps demonstrate the relationship between audit results and compliance\nFinding statuses include: Open, In Progress, Closed, Overdue\nYou can edit your own draft findings but cannot approve or close them\nfindings\nseverity\ncritical\nhigh\nmedium\nlow\nremediation\nrecommendations\nobservations	{0.01509857177734375,0.04718017578125,0.0787353515625,-0.004573822021484375,-0.0338134765625,-0.0177154541015625,0.001687049865722656,-0.066894531