cmn2wa6ne006ljc3o40j5tx1c	ah-audit-settings	internal-audit	Settings	audit	{AuditHead}	How do I configure audit settings?	How do I configure audit settings?\nHow do I set up audit types?\nHow do I configure audit periodicity?\nHow do I manage escalation policies?\nHow do I set up risk assessment matrices for audits?\nHow do I manage audit categories?\nWhere do I configure audit departments?\nHow do I manage nature of controls?\nHow do I manage audit user roles?\nAudit Settings lets you configure the entire audit function including audit types, departments, periodicity, processes, risk assessment matrices, categories, control nature, user management, and escalation policies. As Audit Head, you have exclusive access to all audit configuration.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Settings**\n**Audit Types** — define audit types (internal, external, compliance, operational)\n**Departments** — manage departments relevant to audit scope\n**Periodicity** — configure audit frequency and cycle settings (annual, quarterly, etc.)\n**Process** — define process and sub-process definitions for audit scope\n**Risk Assessment** — configure probability and impact matrices for audit risk assessment\n**Categories** — manage audit categories for classification\n**Nature of Controls** — define control types and characteristics used in audit assessments\n**User Management** — assign audit team members and configure their roles within the audit function\n**Escalation** — set up escalation policies for overdue findings and CAPAs\nAs Audit Head, you are the primary administrator of audit settings — this is NOT available to Auditors or lower roles\nChanges to settings affect all audit activities across the organization\nConfigure escalation policies carefully to ensure timely follow-up on critical findings\nRisk assessment matrices here are specific to the audit function and separate from organization-wide risk settings\naudit settings\naudit types\nperiodicity\nescalation\nrisk assessment\ncategories\nnature of controls\nuser management\nconfiguration	{-0.042083740234375,0.024078369140625,0.079833984375,-0.0303192138671875,-0.048248291015625,-0.007904052734375,0.005550384521484375,-0.032562255859375,0.0438232421875,0.01557159423828125,0.0202484130859375,-0.04815673828125,0.025390625,-0.002016067504882812,0.0219268798828125,-0.01320648193359375,-0.04901123046875,0.034576416015625,0.00691986083984375,0.06378173828125,0.068359375,0.045196533203125,0.01114654541015625,0.044921875,-0.006496429443359375,-0.0401611328125,0.004077911376953125,0.0279998779296875,-0.01287078857421875,-0.01010894775390625,0.0146636962890625,-0.03192138671875,-0.005580902099609375,-0.0125274658203125,0.01326751708984375,0.024871826171875,-0.011688232421875,-0.0213165283203125,0.051666259765625,0.007175445556640625,-0.0061798095703125,-0.0274810791015625,-0.0171966552734375,0.01424407958984375,-0.0161590576171875,0.011993408203125,0.002962112426757812,0.02099609375,-0.032989501953125,0.0105438232421875,-0.02410888671875,0.0341796875,0.03973388671875,-0.002466201782226562,0.0168914794921875,0.03704833984375,-0.0174102783203125,0.00240325927734375,-0.026031494140625,0.01122283935546875,0.02178955078125,-0.07257080078125,-0.0457763671875,-0.037567138671875,0.0146636962890625,-0.0187530517578125,-0.048919677734375,0.0177764892578125,0.006145477294921875,-0.032135009765625,0.019989013671875,0.03106689453125,-0.0200347900390625,-0.041961669921875,0.0052642822265625,-0.0147857666015625,0.049896240234375,0.034210205078125,-0.0227508544921875,0.0294189453125,0.0150909423828125,0.0199127197265625,-0.0675048828125,0.001235008239746094,0.0159759521484375,0.001389503479003906,-0.04864501953125,-0.0122528076171875,-0.017730712890625,-0.043975830078125,-0.0053558349609375,0.021759033203125,-0.048431396484375,0.021331787109375,0.01441192626953125,-0.01922607421875,0.0003342628479003906,-0.024017333984375,0.002439498901367188,0.0246734619140625,0.04541015625,-0.019500732421875,0.0186767578125