cmn2wa6kz006fjc3osl5gj5w9	ah-audit-planning	internal-audit	Planning	audit	{AuditHead}	How do I create and manage audit plans?	How do I create and manage audit plans?\nHow do I create an audit engagement?\nHow do I assign auditors to an engagement?\nHow do I manage the annual audit plan?\nHow do I set audit scope and objectives?\nHow do I link risks to an audit plan?\nHow do I track planned hours?\nHow do I manage audit schedules?\nAudit Planning lets you create and manage audit engagements, define scope and objectives, assign audit team members, link risks, and track planned hours. As Audit Head, you have full control over the entire planning process.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Audit Planning**\nClick **Create** to start a new audit engagement\nEnter engagement details: **title, department, start date, end date, planned hours**\nDefine the **scope and objectives** for the engagement\n**Assign auditors** — select single or multiple team members to the engagement\n**Link risks** from the audit risk register to the engagement for risk-based planning\nSet the engagement status: **Planned, In Progress, Completed, or Cancelled**\nUpload engagement documents and work programs as needed\nUse **search and pagination** to manage engagements\nEdit or delete engagements as plans evolve\nAs Audit Head, you are the primary owner of audit planning — only you and Audit Managers can create engagements\nEnsure risks are linked to engagements for proper risk-based audit coverage\nTrack planned vs actual hours to manage audit team workload effectively\nAuditors assigned here will see their engagements in the Fieldwork module\naudit planning\nengagement\nassign auditors\nannual plan\nscope\nobjectives\nplanned hours\nschedule\naudit team	{-0.00937652587890625,0.04852294921875,0.06298828125,-0.05316162109375,-0.076416015625,-0.037109375,0.001924514770507812,-0.01207733154296875,0.0073699951171875,0.001993179321289062,0.05242919921875,-0.0264892578125,0.047515869140625,-0.0