cmn2wa6m6006ijc3o0t5hn5fv	ah-audit-capa	internal-audit	CAPA Tracking	audit	{AuditHead}	How do I manage CAPA tracking?	How do I manage CAPA tracking?\nHow do I create a CAPA?\nHow do I track corrective actions?\nHow do I track preventive actions?\nHow do I escalate overdue CAPAs?\nHow do I verify CAPA effectiveness?\nHow do I monitor CAPA implementation?\nWhat is CAPA tracking?\nCAPA Tracking manages Corrective and Preventive Actions arising from audit findings. As Audit Head, you have full control to create CAPAs, assign responsible persons, track implementation, verify effectiveness, and escalate overdue items.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → CAPA Tracking**\nView all CAPA items with **status, severity, and due dates**\nClick **Create** to add a new CAPA linked to a finding\nDefine **corrective actions** (fix the root cause) and **preventive actions** (prevent recurrence)\nEnter action details: **type, description, completion percentage, status**\n**Assign responsible persons** and set **target completion dates**\nTrack **implementation progress** through completion percentage updates\nAdd **comments and discussions** for ongoing communication\nAttach **evidence files** to demonstrate action completion\n**Verify action effectiveness** after implementation\n**Escalate overdue CAPAs** that have missed their target dates\nUse **filters** to view CAPAs by status (Open, In Progress, Closed, Overdue)\nUse **search and pagination** to manage large CAPA inventories\nAs Audit Head, you can escalate overdue CAPAs to management for attention\nRegularly review CAPA status on the Audit Dashboard for department-level visibility\nEffectiveness verification is critical — ensure corrective actions actually resolve the issue\nCAPA data feeds into the Audit Dashboard CAPA status by department chart\nCAPA\ncorrective action\npreventive action\nescalation\neffectiveness\nimplementation\noverdue\nremediation	{-0.0070343017578125,0.049591064453125,0.06561279296875,-0.0066108703