cmn2wa7e2007ajc3ovtagprmp	am-no-access	general	Roles	audit	{AuditManager}	What modules can I NOT access as Audit Manager?	What modules can I NOT access as Audit Manager?\nWhy can't I see Organization settings?\nWhere is Asset Management?\nWhy is GRC Administration hidden?\nWhat is restricted for Audit Manager?\nWhy can't I access Audit Settings?\nWhy can't I see Risk Universe?\nAudit Manager restricted pages\nAs Audit Manager, you do not have access to Organization, Asset Management, GRC Administration, Audit Settings, or Audit Universe/Risk Universe. Your access covers Internal Audit (full CRUD) and Compliance/Risk Management (view-only).\nYour sidebar shows **Internal Audit** (full access), **Compliance**, and **Risk Management** (view-only)\n**Organization** (profile, users, processes, BIA) is not accessible — managed by Customer Administrator\n**Asset Management** (inventory, classification) is not accessible — managed by asset management roles\n**GRC Administration** (customer accounts, email, configuration) is not accessible — managed by GRC Administrator\n**Audit Settings** (types, departments, periodicity, escalation policies) is not accessible — managed by Audit Head\n**Audit Universe / Risk Universe** configuration is not accessible — managed by Audit Head\nCompliance and Risk Management modules are **view-only** — you can browse but not create, edit, or delete records\nIf you need changes in restricted modules, contact the Audit Head or appropriate module owner\nThis is by design — the Audit Manager role focuses on executing and managing audit engagements\nThe Audit Head has broader access including Settings and Universe configuration\nView-only access to Compliance and Risk provides context for audit planning without creating conflicts of interest\nMenu items are hidden based on your permissions; restricted pages cannot be accessed even by URL\nno access\nrestricted\nunavailable\norganization\nasset management\nadministration\nhidden\nsettings\nrisk univ