cmn2wa7fv007fjc3ol1f2jb5o	am-audit-planning	internal-audit	Audit Planning	audit	{AuditManager}	How do I create and manage audit engagements as Audit Manager?	How do I create and manage audit engagements as Audit Manager?\nHow do I plan an audit?\nWhere do I create audit engagements?\nHow do I assign auditors to an engagement?\nHow do I manage the annual audit plan?\nWhere is audit planning?\nHow do I set audit scope and objectives?\nHow do I link risks to audit plans?\nHow do I track engagement status?\nAudit Planning lets you create and manage audit engagements, define scope and objectives, assign audit team members, link risks, and track planned hours. This is a core management capability for Audit Managers.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Audit Planning**\nClick **Create** to start a new audit engagement\nEnter engagement details: **title, department, start/end dates**\nDefine the **scope and objectives** of the engagement\n**Assign auditors** (single or multiple) to the engagement\n**Link risks** from the audit risk register to the plan\nSet **planned hours** for the engagement\nTrack **engagement status**: Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled\n**Upload engagement documents** such as audit programs or checklists\nUse **search and pagination** to manage multiple engagements\n**Edit or delete** engagements as needed\nYou can assign multiple auditors to a single engagement\nLinking risks to engagements supports risk-based audit planning\nTrack planned hours vs actual hours to improve future estimations\nCheck the auditor schedule on the Dashboard before assigning to avoid overloading team members\naudit planning\nengagement\nassign auditors\nannual plan\nscope\nobjectives\ntimeline\nplanned hours	{-0.0152587890625,0.0618896484375,0.057281494140625,-0.05499267578125,-0.072021484375,-0.0241851806640625,-0.003038406372070312,-0.007526397705078125,0.004581451416015625,0.012298583984375,0.047821044921875,-0.030059814453125,0.046630859375,-0.0333251953125