cmn2wa7gf007hjc3onsvtr9ba	am-audit-findings	internal-audit	Findings	audit	{AuditManager}	How do I create and manage audit findings as Audit Manager?	How do I create and manage audit findings as Audit Manager?\nWhere do I document audit findings?\nHow do I classify finding severity?\nHow do I assign finding owners?\nHow do I track finding remediation?\nWhere are audit findings managed?\nHow do I create a finding from fieldwork?\nHow do I link findings to controls?\nThe Findings page lets you document and manage audit findings identified during fieldwork. You can classify severity, assign owners, set remediation due dates, and track resolution progress.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → Fieldwork** and select an engagement, or access findings from the engagement detail\nClick **Create Finding** to document a new finding\nEnter finding details: **finding ID, title, description, and recommendation**\nClassify **severity**: Critical, High, Medium, Low, or Informational\n**Assign a finding owner** responsible for remediation\nSet a **remediation due date**\n**Link the finding to controls and risks** as appropriate\nTrack finding **status**: Open, In Progress, Closed, Overdue\n**Edit or delete** findings as needed\nCritical and High severity findings should be escalated promptly\nFindings are typically created from fieldwork observations and linked to the parent engagement\nEach finding should include a clear recommendation for remediation\nOverdue findings may need escalation — use CAPA tracking for follow-up\nfindings\nseverity\ncritical\nhigh\nmedium\nlow\nremediation\nfinding owner\naudit observations	{0.0063323974609375,0.056304931640625,0.08502197265625,-0.0045013427734375,-0.037017822265625,-0.0192718505859375,0.0007953643798828125,-0.06292724609375,-0.0117340087890625,0.0234832763671875,0.048919677734375,-0.0171661376953125,-0.0086822509765625,-0.030517578125,0.029632568359375,-0.031646728515625,0.0118560791015625,-0.00323486328125,-0.03436279296875,0.05859