cmn2wa7my007ijc3onmft2nbr	am-audit-capa	internal-audit	CAPA Tracking	audit	{AuditManager}	How do I track CAPA items as Audit Manager?	How do I track CAPA items as Audit Manager?\nWhere do I manage corrective actions?\nHow do I create CAPA entries?\nHow do I track CAPA progress?\nHow do I escalate overdue CAPAs?\nWhere is CAPA tracking?\nHow do I verify corrective action effectiveness?\nHow do I link CAPA to findings?\nHow do I manage preventive actions?\nCAPA Tracking lets you manage Corrective and Preventive Actions arising from audit findings. You can create CAPA entries, assign responsible persons, track implementation progress, verify effectiveness, and escalate overdue items.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Internal Audit → CAPA Tracking**\nView all CAPA items with **status, severity, and due dates**\nClick **Create** to add a new CAPA entry linked to a finding\nDefine **corrective and preventive actions** with clear descriptions\nSet **action type, description, completion percentage, and status**\n**Assign responsible persons** and **target completion dates**\nTrack **implementation progress** using completion percentage\nAdd **comments** for discussion and follow-up\nUpload **file attachments** as evidence of corrective action\n**Verify action effectiveness** once actions are completed\n**Escalate overdue CAPAs** to appropriate management\n**Filter** by status to focus on open or overdue items\nEscalating overdue CAPAs is a key Audit Manager responsibility — monitor due dates closely\nEach CAPA should be linked to a specific finding for traceability\nVerify effectiveness before closing a CAPA to ensure the root cause is addressed\nUse the Dashboard CAPA charts to identify departments with persistent overdue actions\nCAPA\ncorrective action\npreventive action\ntracking\nescalation\noverdue\neffectiveness\nremediation	{-0.01357269287109375,0.057647705078125,0.0703125,-0.01025390625,-0.0450439453125,-0.0088958740234375,-0.0071563720703125,-0.052001953125,0.033966064453