cmn2wa8qp008njc3o5c8tz8q3	co-role-overview	general	Roles & Permissions	grc	{Contributor}	What can I do as a Contributor?	What can I do as a Contributor?\nWhat is the Contributor role?\nWhat are my permissions as a Contributor?\nWhat modules can a Contributor access?\nContributor capabilities\nWhat is the difference between Contributor and Department Contributor?\nCan I create records as a Contributor?\nWhat pages can I see as Contributor?\nContributor vs Reviewer\nThe Contributor role has organization-wide access to Compliance, Risk Management, and Asset Management modules. Unlike the Department Contributor (scoped to one department), you can view and contribute to data across ALL departments in the organization.\nYou have **organization-wide** access — not limited to a single department like the Department Contributor\n**Compliance**: View dashboards, frameworks, and risk matrix; create and edit controls, governance documents, evidence, exceptions, and KPIs\n**Risk Management**: View dashboards and settings; create and edit risks in the register, perform risk assessments, create risk response plans, and manage the risk control matrix\n**Asset Management**: View dashboards; create and edit asset classifications\n**Organization**: View, create, and edit business processes\nYou do **NOT** have access to Internal Audit, GRC Administration, Organization Profile, Context, Users, BIA, or Organization Settings\nOrganization-wide scope means you can see and work with data across all departments — this is the key difference from Department Contributor who is limited to their assigned department\nYou can create and edit records but typically cannot delete records or approve/reject submissions — those actions require administrator or reviewer roles\nThe Reviewer role has broader view access (including Internal Audit) but cannot create or edit records — your role is specifically designed for active contribution\nIf a sidebar menu item or action button is not visible, your role does not have the required permission\nPermissions are enforced at both the UI level (hiding unavailable options) and the API level (blocking unauthorized requests)\ncontributor\nrole\npermissions\nscope\norganization-wide\ncreate\nedit\ncapabilities	{0.0173492431640625,0.0350341796875,0.032440185546875,0.059722900390625,0.01678466796875,-0.00421142578125,-0.004283905029296875,0.0214080810546875,0.01471710205078125,0.023956298828125,0.0236968994140625,-0.01499176025390625,0.01010894775390625,-0.0006799697875976562,-0.01369476318359375,0.0386962890625,0.003841400146484375,0.024383544921875,0.016143798828125,0.06341552734375,0.040313720703125,0.0112152099609375,0.00899505615234375,0.0299835205078125,-0.0285797119140625,0.003604888916015625,-0.07257080078125,0.05950927734375,-0.01947021484375,-0.02996826171875,0.01934814453125,-0.01360321044921875,-0.039581298828125,0.0242156982421875,-0.0111541748046875,0.01812744140625,0.00621795654296875,0.0106353759765625,0.022552490234375,0.0219879150390625,-0.004169464111328125,0.04498291015625,-0.00457763671875,0.001908302307128906,-0.00835418701171875,0.0081787109375,-0.029754638671875,-0.0111083984375,0.029937744140625,0.004024505615234375,-0.0208282470703125,0.04107666015625,0.05670166015625,-0.004901885986328125,-0.0265045166015625,-0.0005640983581542969,-0.0199737548828125,-0.01152801513671875,-0.07501220703125,-0.02508544921875,-0.02813720703125,-0.0712890625,-0.0242462158203125,-0.003917694091796875,-0.03125,-0.024322509765625,-0.0252532958984375,0.01424407958984375,-0.01361083984375,0.005321502685546875,0.0152587890625,0.011322021484375,-0.017913818359375,-0.019012451171875,-0.0149688720703125,-0.0129241943359375,0.05340576171875,0.04248046875,-0.04974365234375,-0.0272979736328125,-0.003986358642578125,0.057891845703125,-0.06072998046875,-0.011322021484375,-0.0247955322265625,0.02166748046875,0.00787353515625,-0.002435684204101562,-0.007656097412109375,-0.060546875,-0.04034423828125,-0.014373779296875,-0.034332275390625,