cmn2wa8sq008sjc3o693mx292	co-comp-controls	compliance	Control Assessment	grc	{Contributor}	How do I work with compliance controls as a Contributor?	How do I work with compliance controls as a Contributor?\nHow to assess controls?\nHow to create a new control?\nHow to edit control status?\nCan I edit controls as Contributor?\nHow to link controls to evidence?\nHow to filter controls by framework?\nWhere do I see control assessment status?\nHow to map controls to risks?\nView, create, and edit compliance control assessments across the entire organization. You can assess control effectiveness, link controls to evidence, and map controls to risks — working with data from any department.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Controls**\nView all controls with status indicators: Compliant, Partially Compliant, Non-Compliant, Not Assessed\nUse filters to narrow by **framework**, **domain**, or **status**\nClick **Create** to add a new control — specify code, name, description, domain, and category\nClick on an existing control to **edit** its details or update the assessment status\n**Assess control effectiveness** by setting the appropriate compliance status\n**Link controls to evidence** items to demonstrate compliance\n**Map controls to risks** to show risk coverage and mitigation\nUse **multi-select column filtering** and **search** to find specific controls\nUse **bulk assessment** capabilities for efficient processing of multiple controls\nYour access is organization-wide — you can create and edit controls across all departments, unlike the Department Contributor who is limited to their department\nControl status changes (e.g., moving from Non-Compliant to Compliant) directly affect framework compliance percentages shown on the dashboard\nPagination is available for navigating large control sets\nControls are derived from adopted frameworks — each control maps to specific framework requirements\ncontrol\nassessment\ncompliance\ncompliant\nnon-compliant\nevidence\nedi