cmn2wa8t4008tjc3oulw0fcdv	co-comp-governance	compliance	Governance Documents	grc	{Contributor}	How do I manage governance documents as a Contributor?	How do I manage governance documents as a Contributor?\nHow to create a policy?\nHow to create a governance document?\nHow to edit a procedure?\nHow to upload document attachments?\nHow to set review schedules for policies?\nHow to manage document versions?\nWhere do I manage policies and procedures?\nHow to link documents to frameworks?\nCreate, edit, and manage governance documents (policies, procedures, standards, guidelines) across the organization. Track document lifecycle including creation, review, approval, version history, and link documents to frameworks and controls.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Governance**\nView all governance documents with version and status information\nClick **Create** to add a new document — select the type: Policy, Procedure, Standard, or Guideline\nEnter document properties: **code**, **name**, **version**, and **document type**\n**Edit document content and metadata** as compliance requirements change\n**Upload supporting files and attachments** to documents\n**Set review schedules and due dates** for policy recurrence (e.g., annual review)\n**Assign document owners and reviewers** for the review workflow\n**Link documents to frameworks and controls** for traceability\nTrack **version history** to see how documents have evolved\n**Download documents** for offline reference\nYour access is organization-wide — you can create and edit documents across all departments\nDocument review and approval workflow involves submitting documents for reviewer/administrator approval — as a Contributor you create and edit but approval is typically handled by Reviewers or Administrators\nPolicy recurrence settings trigger reminders when documents are due for review\nVersion history provides an audit trail of all changes made to documents\nEvidence can be attached to governance documents to s