cmn2wa8tx008vjc3ou7xm1ohe	co-comp-exceptions	compliance	Exceptions	grc	{Contributor}	How do I manage compliance exceptions as a Contributor?	How do I manage compliance exceptions as a Contributor?\nHow to create a compliance exception?\nHow to document a risk acceptance?\nHow to request a compensating control exception?\nWhere do I manage exceptions?\nHow to track exception status?\nHow to set exception expiry dates?\nHow to edit an exception?\nDocument and track compliance exceptions — situations where a control cannot be fully implemented. Create exception requests with justification, specify compensating controls, and track approval status across the organization.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Compliance → Exceptions**\nView all compliance exceptions with status indicators\nClick **Create** to add a new exception request\nEnter exception properties: **code**, **description**, and **severity**\nProvide a **justification** explaining why the control cannot be fully implemented\nSpecify any **compensating controls** that partially address the gap\nSet the **exception expiry/target remediation date**\nAssign a **department** and **owner** to the exception\nTrack exception **approval status**: Open, In-Progress, or Closed\n**Link the exception to the relevant control** for traceability\nYour access is organization-wide — you can create and edit exceptions across all departments\nException approval is managed by reviewers or administrators — your role focuses on creating and documenting exceptions\nVisual status indicators (pie chart, status timeline) provide a quick overview of all exceptions\nExceptions should include clear justification and compensating controls to support the risk acceptance decision\nPagination is available for navigating large exception lists\nexception\ncompliance\nrisk acceptance\ncompensating control\ncreate\nedit\nstatus\nexpiry	{0.0159759521484375,0.05609130859375,0.057373046875,0.00804901123046875,-0.02484130859375,-0.0008816719055175781,-0.0203