cmn2wa94m0091jc3obfzlqbgw	co-risk-response	risk-management	Risk Response	grc	{Contributor}	How do I create risk response plans as a Contributor?	How do I create risk response plans as a Contributor?\nHow to define a risk treatment plan?\nHow to set a risk mitigation strategy?\nHow to create action plans for risks?\nHow to track risk response progress?\nWhere do I manage risk treatments?\nHow to assign action owners for risk response?\nWhat risk strategies can I choose?\nPlan and track risk treatment actions across the organization. Define response strategies (Mitigate, Accept, Transfer, Avoid), create action plans, assign owners, and monitor implementation progress.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Risk Management → Risk Response**\nView all risks requiring response or treatment across the organization\nSelect a risk and define the **response strategy**: Mitigate, Accept, Transfer, or Avoid\n**Create treatment action plans** with specific activities and due dates\n**Assign action owners** responsible for implementing each action\nSet **due dates** for each action item\nTrack **action implementation status**: Open, In-Progress, or Completed\nMonitor **response progress** to ensure treatments are on track\n**Document response effectiveness** after implementation\nYour access is organization-wide — you can create and edit risk response plans across all departments\nEach risk can have multiple action items with different owners and due dates\nResponse progress tracking helps ensure timely completion of treatment plans\nThe four treatment strategies align with ISO 31000 risk management standard: Mitigate (reduce), Accept (retain), Transfer (share), Avoid (eliminate)\nrisk response\ntreatment\nmitigation\nstrategy\naction plan\nmitigate\naccept\ntransfer\navoid	{-0.01617431640625,0.02789306640625,0.07086181640625,0.006984710693359375,-0.034088134765625,-0.06878662109375,-0.0187835693359375,0.0278472900390625,0.019500732421875,0.0307769775390625,0.0233612060546875,0.00664520263671