cmn2wa9630095jc3owhwy1p64	co-asset-classification	asset-management	Asset Classification	grc	{Contributor}	How do I manage asset classifications as a Contributor?	How do I manage asset classifications as a Contributor?\nHow to classify an asset?\nHow to create asset classifications?\nHow to set CIA ratings for assets?\nHow to define classification levels?\nWhere do I classify assets?\nHow to organize asset categories?\nHow to edit asset classification?\nWhat is CIA in asset classification?\nClassify assets based on Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability (CIA) requirements across the organization. Create and edit classification hierarchies (Category, Sub-Category, Group) and define protection requirements.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → Asset Management → Classification**\nView the classification hierarchy: **Category → Sub-Category → Group**\nClick **Create** to add a new classification entry\nDefine **classification levels**: Public, Internal, Confidential, or Restricted\nSet **CIA impact ratings** for each classification:\n  - **Confidentiality** — impact if information is disclosed to unauthorized parties\n  - **Integrity** — impact if information is modified without authorization\n  - **Availability** — impact if information or systems become unavailable\nDefine **handling and protection requirements** per classification level\n**Edit** existing classifications as requirements evolve\nUse the **hierarchy view** to see the overall classification structure\nYour access is organization-wide — you can create and edit classifications across all departments\nCIA stands for Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability — the three pillars of information security\nClassification levels should align with your organization's information security policy\nProper asset classification is essential for risk management — it determines what protection controls are required\nAsset inventory management (creating/editing individual assets) is managed through the Inventory page by administrators\nasset\nclassification\nCIA\nconfidentiality\nintegrity\navailability\ncategory\ncreate\nedit	{-0.0150299072265625,0.02166748046875,0.04638671875,0.00860595703125,-0.002452850341796875,-0.00646209716796875,0.002288818359375,-0.0184173583984375,-0.0004935264587402344,0.01165771484375,0.038604736328125,-0.021148681640625,0.0216217041015625,-0.01506805419921875,-0.00876617431640625,-0.0096588134765625,-0.004230499267578125,0.042572021484375,-0.0275115966796875,0.0289764404296875,-0.002727508544921875,0.039794921875,-0.02392578125,0.027069091796875,-0.0277862548828125,0.002706527709960938,-0.01177215576171875,-0.01163482666015625,-0.0272216796875,0.0097503662109375,0.08758544921875,-0.006801605224609375,-0.0112152099609375,-0.0001740455627441406,0.005046844482421875,0.02069091796875,0.00705718994140625,-0.002145767211914062,0.0236358642578125,0.03289794921875,-0.056488037109375,0.016021728515625,-0.003482818603515625,-0.0450439453125,-0.015472412109375,-0.026275634765625,-0.0206756591796875,-0.005615234375,-0.0205841064453125,-0.0269317626953125,-0.055999755859375,0.033538818359375,0.0244140625,0.0282745361328125,-0.040283203125,0.03338623046875,-0.02508544921875,0.0316162109375,-0.05511474609375,0.00525665283203125,-0.003774642944335938,-0.039215087890625,0.0279083251953125,0.0236663818359375,-0.0241851806640625,-0.03533935546875,-0.035186767578125,0.01273345947265625,-0.0008363723754882812,-0.043792724609375,0.0217437744140625,0.0153961181640625,-0.0225830078125,0.006893157958984375,-0.0261077880859375,-0.013763427734375,-0.03662109375,0.0295562744140625,-0.0050811767578125,-0.020843505859375,-0.001825332641601562,0.01387786865234375,-0.0592041015625,-0.01275634765625,0.011627197265625,-0.01139068603515625,-0.043121337890625,-0.0225067138671875,-0.062255859375,-0.06390380859375,-0.028289794921875,0.06304931640625,-0.048828125,0.017730712890625,-0.011962890625,-0.0222625732421875,0.00948333740234375,0.00542449951171875,-0.04083251953125,0.013671875,-0.00239