cmn2wa9c90096jc3owxxgm6s5	gen-roles-overview	general	Roles & Permissions	both	{}	What are all the roles and how do they compare?	What are all the roles and how do they compare?\nRole comparison table\nDifferences between all roles\nWhich role has what access?\nCompare Contributor vs Reviewer vs Department roles\nRole hierarchy\nWhat role should I have?\nList all GRC roles\nRole matrix\nWho can create and who can only view?\nThe application has 10 roles ranging from system administrators to department-scoped contributors. Here is a comprehensive comparison of every role, their scope, and key capabilities.\n**GRC Administrator** — System-level admin with full access to ALL modules across ALL tenants. Manages customer accounts, compliance master data, email, SSO, and system configuration.\n**Customer Administrator** — Organization-level admin with full CRUD across Organization, Compliance, Risk Management, Asset Management, and Internal Audit within their tenant. Manages users, roles, settings, and BIA.\n**Audit Head** — Full CRUD on all Internal Audit pages (Universe, Planning, Fieldwork, Findings, CAPA, Reports, Settings). View-only access to Organization, Compliance, and Risk Management for audit context. No Asset Management or GRC Admin access.\n**Audit Manager** — Manages audit engagements, assigns work, reviews fieldwork, creates findings, tracks CAPA, generates reports. View-only access to Risk and Compliance.\n**Auditor** — Performs audit fieldwork, creates work papers, documents observations, uploads evidence, creates draft findings. View-only access to Compliance controls/evidence.\n**Auditee** — Views findings assigned to them, provides management responses, updates and uploads evidence for CAPA items assigned to them. Most limited Internal Audit role.\n**Reviewer** — Organization-wide view and review access across Organization, Compliance, Risk Management, Asset Management, and Internal Audit. Can approve/reject submissions but limited create/edit capabilities.\n**Contributor** — Organization-wide create and edit access to Compliance (controls, governance, evidence, exceptions, KPIs), Risk Management (register, assessment, response, risk-matrix), Asset Management (classification), and Organization (processes). No Internal Audit or admin access.\n**Department Reviewer** — Same as Reviewer but scoped to their assigned department only. Can only view and review data within their department.\n**Department Contributor** — Same as Contributor but scoped to their assigned department only. Can create and edit records only within their department.\n**Scope matters**: Organization-wide roles (Reviewer, Contributor) see data across all departments. Department-scoped roles (Department Reviewer, Department Contributor) see only their department's data.\n**Create vs. View**: Contributors can create and edit records. Reviewers can view and approve but have limited editing. Auditor roles are focused on the Internal Audit module.\n**No overlap rule**: A user is assigned one role. The role determines both visible sidebar items and available actions on each page.\n**Permissions are enforced at both UI and API levels** — hidden menu items cannot be accessed by direct URL either.\nContact your Customer Administrator to change your assigned role.\nroles\ncomparison\nmatrix\nhierarchy\naccess\ncontributor\nreviewer\ndepartment\nadmin\nauditor\naudit head	{-0.03927599638700485,0.04536798596382141,0.03954840078949928,0.02989036962389946,0.007070174440741539,0.001001401687972248,0.009856144897639751,0.005825774278491735,0.02130958065390587,0.02005898952484131,0.02585380896925926,-0.03036088868975639,0.01695108413696289,0.00767689710482955,-0.001172429299913347,-0.002750372281298041,-0.02082667872309685,-0.003624857403337955,-0.01655485667288303,0.07602604478597641,0.06002838164567947,-0.006995881907641888,0.01048763189464808,0.0141898775473237,-0.02577951550483704,0.0090760737657547,-0.02989036962389946,0.05829488858580589,-0.03018753975629807,