cmn2wa9xy009wjc3ohl6zlxkj	tprm-vendor-monitoring	tprm	Monitoring & Scanning	tprm	{}	How do I use Vendor Monitoring and trigger scans?	How do I use Vendor Monitoring and trigger scans?\nVendor security monitoring page\nHow to trigger a vendor scan\nMonitoring scorecard with KPIs\nWhat KPIs are tracked in vendor monitoring?\nHow to scan a vendor's security posture\nVendor monitoring dashboard with security scores\nHow does the AI-powered vendor scan work?\nVendor Monitoring provides automated security scanning and continuous monitoring with a 14-KPI scorecard. Trigger on-demand scans that use AI-powered web intelligence gathering with 17+ targeted searches per vendor to assess security posture.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Monitoring**\nView **stat cards**: Vendors Monitored, Avg Security Score, High Risk Vendors, Active Scans\nReview the **Vendor Scorecard** table with 14 KPI columns (sticky vendor name column for horizontal scrolling)\nKPI columns include: Network Security, DNS Health, Patching Cadence, Endpoint Security, IP Reputation, Application Security, Cubit Score, Email Security, SSL/TLS Config, Privacy, Known Breach, Hacker Chatter, Information Leak, Social Engineering\nView **Security Score badges** per vendor with color coding\nTo trigger a new scan, click **Trigger Scan** and enter the vendor name and domain URL\nThe scan runs in two phases: HTTP header scan + 17 web searches + GPT-4o AI assessment\nMonitor scan progress with Queued/Processing indicators (background polling at 10-second intervals)\nClick a vendor to drill into detailed domain scores: Data Breaches, Vulnerabilities, Security Posture, Certifications, DNS/Email, SSL/TLS, IP Reputation, Privacy, Dark Web, News\nView scan history per vendor or delete monitoring records\nKPI cell colors: Green (score ≥80), Emerald (≥65), Yellow (≥50), Red (<50)\nStale scans are automatically cleaned up after 10 minutes\nOnly completed assessments appear in the scorecard\nScans use AI-powered web intelligence — results may take a few minutes to complete\nmonitoring\nscan\nsecurity\nscorecard\nkpi\nvendor\nnetwork security\ndns\nssl\nbreach\nai\nintelligence	{-0.041900634765625,0.03533935546875,0.061279296875,-0.008758544921875,0.003376007080078125,-0.01184844970703125,-0.055328369140625,0.00608062744140625,0.02410888671875,0.01361083984375,0.00943756103515625,-0.032928466796875,-0.028289794921875,-0.0158233642578125,0.04510498046875,-0.035247802734375,-0.0241546630859375,0.0196990966796875,-0.05255126953125,0.02862548828125,0.0599365234375,0.04290771484375,-0.01346588134765625,0.0003399848937988281,-0.0538330078125,0.0257568359375,-0.029205322265625,-0.01556396484375,0.0189666748046875,-0.01404571533203125,0.03857421875,-0.025360107421875,-0.014923095703125,0.0204315185546875,-0.02001953125,0.004428863525390625,-0.028228759765625,-0.0153961181640625,-0.002071380615234375,0.0087738037109375,-0.00333404541015625,0.04669189453125,0.003019332885742188,0.04937744140625,0.01251220703125,-0.002767562866210938,-0.0192108154296875,-0.033203125,-0.020416259765625,-0.00882720947265625,-0.024810791015625,0.034210205078125,-0.0296783447265625,0.007534027099609375,-0.0401611328125,0.0009365081787109375,0.01580810546875,0.0208740234375,-0.034423828125,0.038421630859375,0.0120086669921875,-0.043182373046875,-0.005962371826171875,-0.0191650390625,0.0193023681640625,3.331899642944336e-05,-0.0204315185546875,0.0233612060546875,0.00983428955078125,-0.0716552734375,0.04278564453125,0.0440673828125,0.035308837890625,-0.0050048828125,0.0289764404296875,0.00666046142578125,0.031341552734375,0.017669677734375,-0.005161285400390625,0.04913330078125,0.01123809814453125,-0.0270233154296875,-0.040618896484375,0.006793975830078125,-0.01519012451171875,-0.03436279296875,-0.06512451171875,-0.01837158203125,0.00740814208984375,0.036285400390625,-0.032745361328125,0.005889892578125,-0.009490966796875,0.003902435302734375,0.0255584716796875,-0.008697509765625,-0.01271820068359375,-0.01004791259765625,-0.