cmn2waahv00acjc3oysrf9e6f	tprm-roles-overview	tprm	Roles & Permissions	tprm	{}	What are the TPRM roles and their responsibilities?	What are the TPRM roles and their responsibilities?\nTPRM user roles overview\nWhat roles exist in TPRM?\nWho can do what in TPRM?\nTPRM permissions by role\nList all TPRM roles\nWhat is the difference between RM, BO, and Assessor roles?\nTPRM role descriptions\nTPRM has 11 specialized roles: Administrator, Business Owner, Relationship Manager, Assessor, Approver, Auditor, Account Manager, Subject Matter Expert, Factory Administrator, Factory Assessor, and Internal IT Team. Each role has specific access areas and capabilities.\n**TPRM Administrator** — Full access to all TPRM modules including Vendor Management, Control Center, Program Monitor, User Management, and Configuration\n**Business Owner (BO)** — Manages vendor inventory, assessments, contracts (including renewals and offboarding), and issues for their business unit. Has BO Dashboard with 2 charts\n**Relationship Manager (RM)** — Manages vendor lifecycle end-to-end: creates vendors, initiates assessments, assigns assessors, tracks issues, manages contracts. Has RM Dashboard with 2 charts\n**TPRM Assessor** — Conducts assessments by answering CAIQ questions with AI assistance, gathers evidence, manages issues, and uses Assessment Factory. Has the most comprehensive dashboard with 6 charts\n**TPRM Approver** — Reviews and approves/rejects submitted assessments with detailed review comments. Dashboard mirrors Assessor Dashboard\n**TPRM Auditor** — Read-only access to assessments, issues, vendors, monitoring, and reports for independent audit review\n**Account Manager (AM)** — Manages assessments (Active/Submitted/Past/Offboard), follow-ups, and SME assignments from a commercial perspective\n**Subject Matter Expert (SME)** — Provides domain expertise during assessments in their area of specialization\n**Factory Administrator** — Manages factory team users, Assessment Factory operations, and factory reports for a specific facility\n**Factory Assessor** — Conducts factory-specific assessments with read-only access to factory reports\n**Internal IT Team** — Manages IT-related vendor issues around IT security, infrastructure, and technology risks\nEach role sees different sidebar menu items based on their permissions\nPermissions are enforced at both UI level (hidden options) and API level (blocked requests)\nPermission actions include: view, create, edit, delete, approve\nPermission scopes include: Global, Department, and Own\nroles\npermissions\nadministrator\nbusiness owner\nrelationship manager\nassessor\napprover\nauditor\naccount manager\nsme\nfactory\nit team	{-0.04583740234375,0.07098388671875,0.07659912109375,0.01389312744140625,0.0004832744598388672,-0.01024627685546875,-0.0132293701171875,0.00223541259765625,0.01629638671875,0.0182952880859375,0.015869140625,-0.0246734619140625,0.0074615478515625,0.0097503662109375,0.01346588134765625,-0.019744873046875,-0.0006175041198730469,0.0132904052734375,-0.0069580078125,0.1015625,0.058624267578125,0.00943756103515625,-0.03948974609375,-0.0192413330078125,-0.01971435546875,0.014923095703125,-0.0308685302734375,0.047637939453125,-0.048614501953125,-0.045684814453125,0.037261962890625,-0.0382080078125,-0.035675048828125,0.004268646240234375,0.036529541015625,-0.01381683349609375,-0.010223388671875,0.0308990478515625,0.025482177734375,0.0147705078125,-0.0301971435546875,0.01143646240234375,-0.0264129638671875,0.027618408203125,-0.04022216796875,0.002071380615234375,0.001717567443847656,0.032501220703125,0.01114654541015625,-0.020904541015625,0.0171356201171875,0.02325439453125,0.01195526123046875,0.029388427734375,-0.01560211181640625,0.01123809814453125,-0.00676727294921875,0.005832672119140625,-0.0283203125,-0.01055908203125,-0.0103759765625,-0.04010009765625,-0.0196685791015625,-0.01383209228515625,-0.003171920776367188,-0.004505157470703125,-0.0723876953125,0.002468109130859375,-0.00247001647949