cmn2waakp00ajjc3owcy34mo3	tca-control-center	tprm	Control Center	tprm	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I configure the Control Center as a TPRM Administrator?	How do I configure the Control Center as a TPRM Administrator?\nHow to set up Due Diligence parameters?\nHow to configure Scorecard thresholds?\nWhat is the Control Center in TPRM?\nHow to change VRR levels and cadence settings?\nHow to configure risk parameters?\nControl Center due diligence and scorecard settings\nHow to set remediation timelines and reminders?\nThe Control Center is your configuration hub for TPRM risk parameters. Configure Due Diligence settings (VRR levels, cadence, remediation timelines) and Scorecard thresholds through editable matrix tables with auto-save.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Control Center**\nSelect the **Due Diligence** tab to configure risk parameters\nEdit VRR levels (Critical, High, Moderate, Low, Nominal) across parameters: VRR, Cadence, Remediation, Reminder, and Due Date\nClick any cell to edit the value inline — changes auto-save with 800ms debounce\nWatch for the **save status indicator** to confirm your changes were saved\nSwitch to the **Scorecard** tab to configure security score thresholds\nSet Score categories (Excellent, Good, Moderate, Low, Nominal) with Security Score threshold values\nColored category headers provide visual differentiation between risk levels\nOnly Customer Administrators can modify Control Center settings — this is a critical configuration area\nDue Diligence settings directly affect how vendors are assessed: cadence determines review frequency, remediation sets the timeline for fixing issues\nChanges take effect immediately after auto-save — be careful when modifying production settings\nScorecard thresholds determine how vendor monitoring scores are categorized\ncontrol center\ndue diligence\nscorecard\nvrr\ncadence\nremediation\nthresholds\nconfiguration	{-0.027557373046875,0.0439453125,0.0794677734375,0.006359100341796875,-0.0199737548