cmn2wabdb00b6jc3op8egneyv	tca-user-management	tprm	User Management	tprm	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I manage TPRM users as a Customer Administrator?	How do I manage TPRM users as a Customer Administrator?\nHow to create TPRM users?\nHow to assign TPRM roles to users?\nHow to activate or deactivate TPRM users?\nWhere to manage TPRM user accounts?\nTPRM user administration and role assignment\nHow to add new users to the TPRM module?\nHow to assign departments to TPRM users?\nAs Customer Administrator, you have full control over TPRM user management — create, edit, delete users, assign roles, manage department assignments, and activate/deactivate accounts.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → User Management**\nView the list of all TPRM users with their roles and status\nClick **Create User** to add a new TPRM user\nFill in user details: name, email, username, and other required fields\n**Assign a TPRM role** (e.g., Relationship Manager, Business Owner, Assessor, Account Manager, Approver, Internal IT)\n**Assign a department** to scope the user's access where applicable\nClick **Save** to create the user account\nTo modify, click **Edit** on an existing user to change their role or details\nUse **Activate/Deactivate** to control user access without deleting accounts\nClick **Delete** to permanently remove a user account\nOnly Customer Administrators can manage TPRM users — other roles cannot access this page\nDeactivating a user prevents login but preserves their historical records and assignments\nRole assignment determines which sidebar menu items and features the user can access\nDepartment assignment is important for roles with department-scoped permissions (e.g., BO, Department-level roles)\nuser management\ncreate user\nassign role\nactivate\ndeactivate\ntprm users\ndepartment assignment	{-0.0291748046875,0.0662841796875,0.035430908203125,0.0128936767578125,-0.004199981689453125,-0.0235595703125,0.0018310546875,0.04693603515625,0.0184478759765625,0.02447509765625,