cmn2wabfq00bcjc3ondqbv5i8	tca-offboard-review	tprm	Offboarding	tprm	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do I manage vendor offboarding as a TPRM Administrator?	How do I manage vendor offboarding as a TPRM Administrator?\nHow does the vendor offboarding process work?\nHow to review offboard requests?\nWhat is the multi-step offboard approval workflow?\nHow to approve or reject offboarding?\nVendor offboarding review process\nHow to terminate a vendor relationship?\nVendor offboarding follows a multi-step approval workflow (Assessor → RM → BO) with a dedicated review page. As Customer Administrator, you can review and approve offboarding at any stage.\nOffboarding is initiated from the **BO Contracts** page by clicking Start Offboarding on a vendor\nOr access offboard assessments via the **Offboard tab** in BO or AM Assessments\nComplete the **offboard review questionnaire** documenting the reason for termination\nThe request flows through the **multi-step approval workflow**: Assessor review → RM review → BO final approval\nAt each stage, the reviewer can **approve or reject** the offboarding with documented reasons\nUpon final approval, the vendor is marked as Offboarded/Terminated\nAs Customer Administrator, you can approve offboarding at any stage of the workflow regardless of your role assignment\nOffboarding can only be initiated when specific assessment conditions are met (checked automatically)\nThe offboard questionnaire captures critical information about why the vendor relationship is being terminated\nTerminated vendors remain in the system for historical records but are no longer active\noffboarding\noffboard review\napproval workflow\nterminate vendor\noffboard questionnaire\nmulti-step	{-0.04278564453125,0.0704345703125,0.05242919921875,0.033538818359375,-0.035614013671875,0.01419830322265625,-0.0418701171875,-0.026031494140625,0.04913330078125,0.03826904296875,0.0430908203125,-0.05706787109375,-0.04443359375,0.004268646240234375,0.017822265625,-0.0377197265625