cmn2waboy00bijc3osjtclz2d	tca-permissions-reference	tprm	Permissions & Access	tprm	{CustomerAdministrator}	How do TPRM permissions work for the Customer Administrator?	How do TPRM permissions work for the Customer Administrator?\nWhat permissions does the Customer Administrator have?\nHow does the permission system work in TPRM?\nWhat is the resource:action permission pattern?\nWhat are permission scopes (Global, Department, Own)?\nHow are TPRM permissions enforced?\nWhy can't some users see certain menu items?\nTPRM uses a resource:action permission pattern with scopes (Global, Department, Own). As Customer Administrator, you have Global scope with full CRUD + approve permissions on ALL TPRM resources.\n**Permission actions**: view (read-only), create (new records), edit (modify), delete (remove), approve (approve/reject submissions)\n**Permission scopes**: Global (all records), Department (records in user's department), Own (records owned by or assigned to user)\nAs Customer Administrator, your scope is **Global** — you can access all records across the entire organization\nPermissions are enforced at **two levels**: UI-level (hiding unavailable options) and API-level (blocking unauthorized requests)\nEach role determines which **sidebar menu items** are visible and which **actions** are available on each page\nIf a menu item or button is not visible to a user, it means their role does not have the required permission\nCustomer Administrator has the highest permission level in TPRM — all resources, all actions, Global scope\nOther roles (RM, BO, Assessor, AM, Approver) have more limited permissions and scopes\nPermission enforcement at the API level ensures data security regardless of how the application is accessed\nUse the User Management page to assign appropriate roles to team members based on their responsibilities\npermissions\naccess control\nresource action\nscope\nglobal\ndepartment\nown\nrbac\nenforced	{-0.015655517578125,0.0865478515625,0.08367919921875