cmn2wabpc00bjjc3o32r5dmzs	tbo-role-overview	tprm	Role Overview	tprm	{BusinessOwner}	What is the Business Owner role in TPRM?	What is the Business Owner role in TPRM?\nWhat can I do as a Business Owner?\nBusiness Owner role overview\nWhat pages can a BO access in TPRM?\nWhat is the BO role responsible for?\nBusiness Owner capabilities in TPRM\nWhat does the Business Owner manage?\nBO role summary\nThe Business Owner owns vendor relationships from a business perspective. You manage vendor inventory for your business unit, monitor assessment progress, handle contracts (renewals and offboarding), and oversee issue management.\n**BO Dashboard** — View vendor criticality and assessment status charts for your business unit\n**BO Vendor Inventory** — Create, edit, and manage vendors within your business unit with nested accordion details\n**BO Assessments** — Monitor ongoing, completed, and offboard assessments with tabbed navigation\n**BO Contracts** — Track expiring contracts, renew contracts, initiate vendor offboarding, upload/download documents\n**BO Issues** — View and track issues related to your business unit vendors\n**BO User Management** — Manage team users within your business unit\n**BO Monitoring** — View vendor security monitoring scorecard\n**BO Support** — Submit support requests and access help resources\nAll data is scoped to your business unit — you only see vendors and records assigned to your unit\nThis is a business-side role focused on vendor relationship ownership, not technical assessment\nYou can create and edit vendor records but do not conduct technical assessments\nContract lifecycle management (renewals, offboarding) is a key Business Owner responsibility\nbusiness owner\nbo\nrole\noverview\nresponsibilities\ncapabilities\naccess\nvendor relationship	{-0.031585693359375,0.0653076171875,0.05047607421875,0.040496826171875,-0.00873565673828125,-0.01776123046875,-0.010589599609375,0.003292083740234375,0.0142059326171875,0.01959228515625,0.04098510