cmn2wac2i00btjc3o9oed6svp	tbo-create-vendor	tprm	Vendor Management	tprm	{BusinessOwner}	How do I create a new vendor as a Business Owner?	How do I create a new vendor as a Business Owner?\nBO add new vendor\nHow to onboard a vendor as Business Owner\nSteps to create a vendor in BO inventory\nBusiness Owner vendor creation form\nHow to register a new third-party vendor\nBO new vendor onboarding process\nBusiness Owners can create new vendor records from the BO Vendor Inventory page using a multi-section dialog form that captures all essential vendor information for your business unit.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → BO → Vendor Inventory**\nClick the **Create Vendor** button to open the multi-section dialog form\nFill in **Vendor Info**: name, domain, vendor code, and description\nAdd **Contact** details for the vendor's primary contact person\nSelect the **Service Category** that describes what the vendor provides\nAssign the vendor to the appropriate **Department** within your business unit\nConfigure the **Risk Profile** toggles: Access to Network, Cloud, Access to Data, PII\nEnter **Contract Dates**: start date and end date for the vendor agreement\nAdd any relevant **Certifications** the vendor holds (e.g., ISO 27001, SOC 2)\nClick **Save** to create the vendor record\nAll fields should be filled accurately as they affect risk categorization and assessment requirements\nRisk Profile toggles (Access to Network, Cloud, Access to Data, PII) directly influence the vendor's risk rating\nContract dates are important for tracking renewals — they appear on the BO Contracts page\nNew vendors may need to go through an assessment process after creation\nbo\ncreate\nvendor\nnew\nonboard\nform\nbusiness owner\nadd\nregister	{-0.03927087038755417,0.02009347453713417,0.02601182833313942,0.01212599594146013,-0.01416306663304567,-0.0447673462331295,-0.01891221478581429,-0.001835171831771731,-0.006322151981294155,0.01013713981956244,0.04785308614373207,-0.003802934195846319,0.002