cmn2wac3o00bvjc3oy90mvh1y	tbo-vendor-offboarding	tprm	Contract Management	tprm	{BusinessOwner}	How do I initiate vendor offboarding as a Business Owner?	How do I initiate vendor offboarding as a Business Owner?\nBO vendor offboarding process\nHow to terminate a vendor relationship\nSteps to start offboarding a vendor\nBusiness Owner offboarding workflow\nHow to end a vendor contract\nBO offboard request submission\nBusiness Owners initiate vendor offboarding from the BO Contracts page by clicking Start Offboarding on the vendor's contract. This triggers an offboarding assessment workflow that routes through the BO Assessments offboard tab.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → BO → Contracts**\nLocate the vendor contract you want to offboard\nClick the **Start Offboarding** button on the contract row (this is conditional on the vendor's assessment status)\nThe vendor's status changes to show an **'Offboard Request Submitted'** badge\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → BO → Assessments** and select the **Offboard Assessments** tab\nReview the offboarding assessment in the **Offboard Approval** sub-tab\nClick the offboard assessment to access the **Offboard Review** page for final approval\nOnce approved, the vendor moves to the **Terminated Vendors** sub-tab\nOffboarding can only be initiated when the vendor's current assessment status permits it\nThe offboarding process includes an assessment to ensure proper closure of the vendor relationship\nTerminated vendors remain visible in the Terminated Vendors sub-tab for audit trail purposes\nOffboarding is a significant business decision — ensure all contractual obligations are fulfilled before initiating\nbo\noffboarding\nterminate\nvendor\nend\ncontract\noffboard\nbusiness owner\nrequest	{-0.03454871103167534,0.04762500897049904,0.04400315880775452,0.03779426589608192,-0.05653852969408035,0.009560279548168182,-0.0543748252093792,-0.02742259949445724,0.05169371515512466,0.01705092936754227,0.06105408817529678,-0.05117630586028099