cmn2wac4h00bxjc3okfr3eh4y	trm-role-overview	tprm	Role Overview	tprm	{RelationshipManager}	What is the Relationship Manager role in TPRM?	What is the Relationship Manager role in TPRM?\nWhat can I do as a Relationship Manager?\nRelationship Manager role overview\nWhat pages can an RM access in TPRM?\nWhat is the RM role responsible for?\nRelationship Manager capabilities in TPRM\nWhat does the Relationship Manager manage?\nRM role summary\nThe Relationship Manager owns the vendor lifecycle end-to-end. You create vendors, initiate assessments, assign assessors, track issues with remediation, manage contracts, and ensure vendor compliance throughout the engagement.\n**RM Dashboard** — View vendor criticality distribution and assessment status charts across all managed vendors\n**RM Vendor Inventory** — Create, edit, and manage vendor records with risk ratings and assessment history\n**RM Assessments** — Initiate assessments, assign assessors, and track the full assessment lifecycle from Draft to Completed\n**RM Issue Register** — Track issues with severity, assign remediation owners, set due dates, and add comments\n**RM Contracts** — Manage vendor contracts, track expiration dates, and monitor renewals\n**RM Monitoring** — View vendor security monitoring scorecard with 14 KPI columns\n**Reports** — Generate TPRM reports for vendor risk summaries, assessment completion, and issue resolution\n**RM Support** — Submit support requests and access help resources\nThis is the primary vendor lifecycle management role — you oversee vendors from onboarding through offboarding\nYou create vendors and initiate assessments but do not conduct the technical assessment questionnaire (that is the Assessor's role)\nIssue remediation tracking is a key RM responsibility — assign owners, set due dates, and follow up\nContract management includes tracking expiration dates and ensuring timely renewals\nrelationship manager\nrm\nrole\noverview\nresponsibilities\ncapabilities\naccess\nvendor 