cmn2waccy00c2jc3o6g8l20qi	trm-rm-contracts	tprm	Contract Management	tprm	{RelationshipManager}	How do I manage vendor contracts as a Relationship Manager?	How do I manage vendor contracts as a Relationship Manager?\nRM Contracts page overview\nHow to track contract expiration dates\nHow to renew a vendor contract\nHow to download contract documents\nContract management for Relationship Manager\nHow to monitor contract renewals in TPRM\nVendor contract lifecycle management\nThe RM Contracts page lets you track and manage vendor contracts, monitor expiration dates, handle renewals, and download contract documents to ensure continuous vendor compliance.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → RM → Contracts**\nView the contract listing showing vendor name, contract dates, and current status\nMonitor **expiration dates** — contracts nearing expiration are highlighted for attention\nTrack **contract renewal** status and initiate renewals before contracts expire\nClick **Download** to retrieve contract documents for review\nReview contract terms and conditions to ensure vendor compliance with agreed obligations\nCoordinate with vendors on contract renewals and amendments as needed\nContract management is a key RM responsibility — expired contracts can create compliance gaps\nMonitor expiration dates proactively to allow sufficient time for renewal negotiations\nContract documents can be downloaded for offline review and stakeholder distribution\nContract status ties into the overall vendor lifecycle — active contracts keep vendors in good standing\nrm\ncontract\nexpiration\nrenewal\ndownload\ndocument\nvendor\nrelationship manager\ntracking\nlifecycle	{-0.05143805965781212,0.05349741503596306,0.05509913340210915,0.01235611829906702,-0.02581055648624897,0.002715771785005927,-0.03670224547386169,-0.01466716919094324,0.02007869072258472,0.03983704000711441,-0.002898825332522392,-0.05281096324324608,0.01178407575935125,-0.01243620365858078,0.01645194180309772,-0.00773401465266943,0.0