cmn2wacdc00c3jc3oddffarbj	trm-rm-monitoring	tprm	Monitoring & Scanning	tprm	{RelationshipManager}	How do I use the Vendor Monitoring page as a Relationship Manager?	How do I use the Vendor Monitoring page as a Relationship Manager?\nHow to view vendor security scores\nRM Monitoring scorecard\nHow to trigger a vendor security scan\nWhat KPIs are tracked in vendor monitoring?\nHow to check vendor security posture\nVendor monitoring dashboard for RM\nHow to scan a vendor for security risks\nWhat does the monitoring scorecard show?\nThe Vendor Monitoring page provides a continuous security monitoring scorecard for all monitored vendors. You can view 14 KPI scores, trigger on-demand security scans, and track vendor security posture over time.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → RM → Monitoring**\nView **stat cards** at the top: Vendors Monitored, Avg Security Score, High Risk Vendors, and Active Scans\nReview the **Vendor Scorecard** table with 14 KPI columns per vendor (Network Security, DNS Health, Patching Cadence, Endpoint Security, IP Reputation, Application Security, Cubit Score, Email Security, SSL/TLS Config, Privacy, Known Breach, Hacker Chatter, Information Leak, Social Engineering)\nKPI cells are color-coded: **Green (80+)**, **Emerald (65+)**, **Yellow (50+)**, **Red (<50)** for quick risk identification\nClick **Trigger Scan** to initiate a new vendor scan — enter the vendor name and domain URL\nThe scan runs in two phases: HTTP header scan + 17 web intelligence searches + GPT-4o AI assessment\nMonitor scan progress with **Queued/Processing** status indicators that poll every 10 seconds\nClick a vendor row to view **detailed scan results** with full domain score breakdowns\nView **scan history** per vendor to track security posture trends over time\nOnly completed assessments appear in the scorecard — scans in progress are shown separately\nScans that take longer than 10 minutes are automatically cleaned up as stale\nThe 14 KPIs cover comprehensive security areas from network security to social engineering risk\nUse monitoring data to identify vendors whose security posture has degraded and may need reassessment\nYou can delete vendor monitoring records if they are no longer needed\nrm\nmonitoring\nscan\nsecurity\nscorecard\nkpi\nnetwork security\ndns\nssl\nvendor\nposture\nscore\nrelationship manager	{-0.02823800221085548,0.04011862725019455,0.06729893386363983,0.003231504932045937,-0.009703738614916801,-0.005208534188568592,-0.0336986631155014,-0.006395366508513689,0.009568451903760433,0.009390119463205338,0.001681858440861106,-0.03982345387339592,-0.03209982067346573,0.007034902926534414,0.06169068813323975,-0.03374785557389259,-0.01575473882257938,0.02155976369976997,-0.04230780899524689,0.05317993089556694,0.06621664017438889,0.06611824780702591,-0.004559773486107588,-0.003812622278928757,-0.04592365026473999,0.0448167584836483,-0.02125229500234127,0.008787479251623154,0.03298533335328102,-0.01710760593414307,0.03332969918847084,-0.0428735539317131,0.005017902702093124,0.0243269894272089,-0.01202820800244808,0.001807920867577195,-0.02340458147227764,-0.01120418962091208,-0.01244636718183756,0.01341797038912773,-0.003778800601139665,0.05057258903980255,0.01371314190328121,0.05445900559425354,0.01725519075989723,0.01266774535179138,-0.01655416004359722,-0.02764766104519367,0.009008857421576977,-0.03055017441511154,-0.02690973505377769,0.01881713606417179,-0.02383503876626492,0.008436963893473148,-0.008406217209994793,0.01189292222261429,0.0318046510219574,0.01559485495090485,-0.03170625865459442,0.01640657521784306,0.0373636968433857,-0.02868075855076313,-0.0220763124525547,-0.01527508720755577,0.01614830084145069,-0.002828719792887568,-0.0463172122836113,0.01286452542990446,0.003176160389557481,-0.04885075986385345,0.02742628380656242,0.02061275765299797,0.03866736963391304,0.005912639200687408,0.03581405058503151,0.002281423890963197,0.06055920198559761,0.009925116784870625,-0.02246987447142601,0.03382164984941483,0.0