cmn2wack100c9jc3ouf6tjgqb	tas-assessor-dashboard	tprm	Dashboard	tprm	{TPRMAssessor}	How do I use the Assessor Dashboard?	How do I use the Assessor Dashboard?\nWhat does the Assessor Dashboard show?\nAssessor home page\nHow to see assessment analytics as Assessor?\nAssessor Dashboard charts overview\nWhere do I see issue status and risk charts?\nAssessor analytics dashboard\nWhat are the 6 charts on the Assessor Dashboard?\nThe Assessor Dashboard provides 6 analytical charts — Issue Status, Assessment Progress, Inherent Risk, Assessment Result, Top 5 Vendors by severity, and Domain Distribution — giving you the most comprehensive at-a-glance view of your assessment workload and vendor risk posture.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Assessor → Dashboard**\nView the **Issue Status** bar chart showing Open, Overdue, and Closed issue counts (DB statuses are mapped to these 3 buckets)\nView the **Assessment Progress** bar chart showing Initiated, In Progress, and Completed assessment counts\nView the **Inherent Risk** pie chart breaking down vendors by High, Medium, and Low risk (mapped from VRR levels)\nView the **Assessment Result** pie chart showing Satisfactory, Unsatisfactory, and Deficient outcomes\nView the **Top 5 Vendors** stacked bar chart showing the top 5 vendors ranked by issue severity (High, Medium, Low)\nView the **Domain Distribution** horizontal bar chart showing the top 10 domains by issue count (strips CUST. prefix for readability)\nHover over any chart element for **interactive tooltips** with exact counts\nEach chart handles empty state gracefully — if no data exists for a chart, an appropriate message is displayed\nThe dashboard auto-refreshes data on page load so you always see the latest status\nUse the Issue Status chart to identify overdue items requiring immediate attention\nThe Top 5 Vendors chart helps prioritize which vendor relationships carry the most risk\nDomain Distribution helps you understand which security domains have the most issues 