cmn2waclo00cdjc3o1i4hoxlg	tas-issue-register	tprm	Issue & Remediation	tprm	{TPRMAssessor}	How do I use the Assessor Issue Register?	How do I use the Assessor Issue Register?\nHow to view assessment issues?\nWhere do I see vendor issues by severity?\nIssue register grouped by vendor\nHow to add remediation comments to issues?\nAssessor issue tracking\nHow to check overdue issues?\nIssue severity breakdown by vendor\nThe Assessor Issue Register shows issues identified during assessments, grouped by vendor with High/Medium/Low severity breakdowns. Drill into vendor-specific issues to see details, add remediation comments, and track resolution status.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Assessor → Issue Register**\nView the **issue register tab** showing vendors grouped with High, Medium, and Low severity counts and totals\nClick on a **vendor name** to drill into that vendor's detailed issues list\nView issue details including **domain, severity, issue description, risk, and recommendation**\nCheck each issue's **status** (Open, Overdue, or Closed) and **due date**\nView the **assessment code** linking each issue back to its source assessment\nSee the **question number reference** to identify exactly which CAIQ question raised the issue\nAdd **remediation comments** to issues to document corrective actions or progress updates\nIssues are automatically created during assessments when questions receive unsatisfactory or deficient ratings\nThe severity breakdown (High/Medium/Low) on the vendor list helps you quickly identify the most problematic vendors\nOverdue issues should be prioritized — check the Issue Status chart on your dashboard for a quick overview\nRemediation comments provide an audit trail of actions taken to resolve each issue\nIssue codes and assessment code linkage help maintain traceability between issues and their source assessments\nissue\nregister\nseverity\nhigh\nmedium\nlow\nvendor\nremediation\ncomments\noverdue\nopen\nclosed\ndomain\nassessment	{-0.03