cmn2wacna00chjc3oww7ryvq1	tas-monitoring	tprm	Monitoring	tprm	{TPRMAssessor}	How do I view vendor monitoring as an Assessor?	How do I view vendor monitoring as an Assessor?\nVendor security monitoring scorecard\nHow to see vendor KPI scores?\nMonitoring dashboard for Assessor\nWhere do I see vendor security posture?\n14 KPI monitoring columns\nHow to view vendor scan results?\nVendor monitoring scorecard explanation\nThe Monitoring page displays a vendor security scorecard with 14 KPI columns measuring areas like Network Security, DNS Health, SSL/TLS Config, and more. Each KPI is scored 0-100 with color-coded cells to quickly identify weak areas.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Assessor → Monitoring**\nView the **stat cards** at the top: Vendors Monitored, Avg Security Score, High Risk Vendors, Active Scans\nBrowse the **Vendor Scorecard table** with a sticky vendor name column for easy scrolling\nReview the **14 KPI columns**: Network Security, DNS Health, Patching Cadence, Endpoint Security, IP Reputation, Application Security, Cubit Score, Email Security, SSL/TLS Config, Privacy, Known Breach, Hacker Chatter, Information Leak, Social Engineering\nCheck the **Security Score badge** per vendor with color coding for quick risk identification\nNote the **KPI cell colors**: Green (score 80+), Emerald (65+), Yellow (50+), Red (below 50)\nClick on a vendor to view **detailed KPI breakdown** and scan history\nMonitoring scans are triggered by administrators or Relationship Managers — as an Assessor, you have read-only access to the scorecard\nOnly completed scans appear in the scorecard — in-progress scans show as Queued/Processing\nThe scorecard uses a two-phase intelligence approach: HTTP header scan followed by 17 web searches and GPT-4o assessment\nUse monitoring data to inform your assessment responses — poor KPI scores may warrant additional scrutiny during assessments\nThe 14 KPIs provide a comprehensive view of a vendor's technical security posture beyond what questionnaires reveal\nmonitoring\nscorecard\nkpi\nsecurity\nscan\nvendor\nnetwork\ndns\nssl\npatching\nendpoint\nemail\nbreach\nposture	{-0.020355224609375,0.0149688720703125,0.07073974609375,0.0115203857421875,0.0062713623046875,-0.01450347900390625,-0.052581787109375,-0.0379638671875,0.03411865234375,-8.58306884765625e-06,0.0108489990234375,-0.051605224609375,-0.01288604736328125,-0.00954437255859375,0.0615234375,-0.0411376953125,0.0019378662109375,0.005123138427734375,-0.045440673828125,0.04376220703125,0.05322265625,0.0325927734375,-0.01629638671875,0.004665374755859375,-0.04425048828125,0.01387786865234375,-0.054901123046875,-0.01531982421875,0.0237884521484375,-0.01233673095703125,0.0296783447265625,-0.02410888671875,-0.00432586669921875,0.03668212890625,0.00742340087890625,0.00978851318359375,-0.0297698974609375,0.0025634765625,-0.004322052001953125,0.001287460327148438,-0.00579833984375,0.07000732421875,-0.0181732177734375,0.042572021484375,0.004245758056640625,0.01303863525390625,0.002832412719726562,-0.0224761962890625,-0.0114898681640625,-0.006618499755859375,-0.024505615234375,0.06854248046875,0.003902435302734375,0.0133819580078125,-0.0193023681640625,0.013702392578125,0.016845703125,0.01100921630859375,-0.05560302734375,0.003561019897460938,0.0288848876953125,-0.02764892578125,-0.031097412109375,0.003650665283203125,0.033111572265625,-0.00466156005859375,-0.02099609375,0.0216827392578125,0.00920867919921875,-0.045013427734375,0.047698974609375,0.04901123046875,0.0260009765625,-0.006610870361328125,0.0247650146484375,-0.0206146240234375,0.04425048828125,0.0114593505859375,-0.016204833984375,0.035919189453125,0.003875732421875,-0.01110076904296875,-0.0411376953125,0.001074790954589844,0.01324462890625,-0.0390625,-0.057037353515625,-0.0139617919921875,0.0169525146484375,0.0237274169921875,-0.0269317626953125,0.006397247314453125,-0.001728057861328125,0.002157211303710938,0.025482177734375,0.0216064453125,-0.03131103515625,-0.0211639404296875,-0.04953002929