cmn2wacw300cnjc3ov4ywrh80	tap-role-overview	tprm	Role Overview	tprm	{TPRMApprover}	What is the TPRM Approver role?	What is the TPRM Approver role?\nWhat can I do as an Approver?\nApprover role overview\nWhat pages can an Approver access in TPRM?\nWhat is the Approver responsible for?\nApprover capabilities in TPRM\nWhat does the TPRM Approver do?\nApprover role summary\nThe TPRM Approver is the quality gate for vendor assessments. You review submitted assessments for quality, accuracy, and completeness, then approve or reject them with detailed review comments. This is a focused role with access to only 4 areas: Dashboard, Assessments, Reports, and Notifications.\n**Approver Dashboard** — View 6 analytical charts covering issues, assessments, risk levels, results, top vendors, and domain distribution (same layout as Assessor Dashboard)\n**Approver Assessments** — Review submitted assessments, examine all responses and evidence, view overall scores, and approve or reject with detailed comments\n**Reports** — Generate TPRM reports including vendor risk summaries, assessment completion, and issue resolution tracking\n**Notifications** — Receive alerts when assessments are submitted for your approval, with badge count in the header\nThis is a quality gate / approval role — you do NOT conduct assessments, manage vendors, or configure the system\nYour primary workflow: receive notification → review assessment → approve or reject with comments\nRejected assessments are returned to the assessor for revision and resubmission\nApproved assessments move to Completed status and finalize the assessment lifecycle\nThe Approver Dashboard shares the same 6-chart layout as the Assessor Dashboard\napprover\nrole\noverview\nresponsibilities\ncapabilities\naccess\napprove\nreject\nreview\nquality gate\nassessment approval	{-0.01184844970703125,0.053558349609375,0.035003662109375,0.01413726806640625,-0.0196990966796875,-0.0223541259765625,-0.00873565673828125,0.020721435546875,0.0283966