cmn2wacxb00cqjc3o3hi4uvwa	tap-assessment-scores	tprm	Assessment Management	tprm	{TPRMApprover}	How do I interpret assessment scores and results?	How do I interpret assessment scores and results?\nWhat do assessment scores mean?\nHow is the overall assessment result calculated?\nHow to read assessment result summary?\nWhat is Satisfactory vs Unsatisfactory vs Deficient?\nHow to evaluate vendor risk from assessment scores?\nUnderstanding CAIQ assessment scoring\nAssessment scores are calculated from individual CAIQ question compliance ratings aggregated across domains. The overall result categorizes the vendor as Satisfactory, Unsatisfactory, or Deficient based on their total score.\nOpen an assessment from **Sidebar → TPRM → Approver → Assessments**\nView the **assessment result summary** section showing the overall score and result category\n**Satisfactory** — The vendor meets compliance requirements across assessed domains\n**Unsatisfactory** — The vendor has notable gaps that require attention but may be manageable with remediation\n**Deficient** — The vendor has significant compliance failures requiring immediate action or vendor replacement\nReview **domain-level scores** to identify specific areas of strength or weakness\nCheck individual question responses for detailed evidence supporting the scores\nUse the overall result to inform your approve/reject decision and review comments\nAssessment results reflect the assessor's compliance ratings for each CAIQ question\nDomain-level breakdowns help you pinpoint exactly where a vendor is strong or weak\nWhen rejecting, reference specific low-scoring domains in your comments to guide the assessor\nThe assessment result (Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory/Deficient) feeds into the vendor's overall risk rating on the dashboard\nScores are recalculated if an assessment is rejected and resubmitted with updated responses\nscore\nresult\nsatisfactory\nunsatisfactory\ndeficient\nrating\ncompliance\ndomain\ncaiq\nsummary\noverall	{