cmn2wad4700csjc3o0rzpvx8w	tap-assessment-lifecycle	tprm	Assessment Management	tprm	{TPRMApprover}	What is the assessment lifecycle and where does the Approver fit in?	What is the assessment lifecycle and where does the Approver fit in?\nAssessment status flow for Approver\nWhen does an assessment reach the Approver?\nWhat happens after I approve an assessment?\nWhat happens after I reject an assessment?\nAssessment workflow stages\nHow does the assessment move through statuses?\nWhat is the Submitted to Approved flow?\nAssessments follow a defined lifecycle: Draft → In Progress → Submitted → Under Review → Approved/Completed (or Rejected → returned to assessor). As the Approver, you act at the 'Under Review' stage — you are the final quality gate before an assessment is finalized.\n**Draft** — Assessment created by the RM, not yet started by the assessor\n**In Progress** — Assessor is actively answering CAIQ questions and attaching evidence\n**Submitted** — Assessor has completed and submitted the assessment for review\n**Under Review** — You (Approver) are reviewing the assessment — this is your active stage\n**Approved / Completed** — You approved the assessment, finalizing the vendor's risk evaluation\n**Rejected** — You rejected the assessment with comments; it returns to the assessor for revision\nAfter rejection, the assessor revises and resubmits, bringing it back to Under Review for you again\nThe cycle repeats until the assessment meets quality standards and is approved\nYou only see assessments in the Submitted or Under Review statuses on your Approver Assessments page\nApproved assessments cannot be edited further — they become the official record of the vendor evaluation\nThe assessment status is tracked on the dashboard charts so you can monitor overall progress\nMultiple revision cycles are normal for complex vendor assessments — each cycle improves quality\nStatus changes are recorded in the assessment history for audit trail purposes\nlifecycle\nstat