cmn2wad5e00cvjc3ok1flwvla	tap-approve-reject-guide	tprm	Assessment Management	tprm	{TPRMApprover}	When should I approve vs. reject an assessment?	When should I approve vs. reject an assessment?\nCriteria for approving an assessment\nWhen to reject a vendor assessment?\nWhat to check before approving?\nAssessment quality checklist for Approver\nHow to decide whether to approve or reject?\nWhat makes an assessment ready for approval?\nApprove an assessment when all questions have thorough responses, evidence supports the compliance ratings, and the overall score accurately reflects the vendor's risk posture. Reject when responses are incomplete, evidence is missing or insufficient, or ratings do not match the supporting evidence.\n**Check completeness** — Verify all CAIQ questions in every domain have been answered (no blank or placeholder responses)\n**Verify evidence** — Confirm that evidence documents are attached where required and are relevant to the questions\n**Validate compliance ratings** — Ensure the compliance rating for each question is consistent with the response text and evidence\n**Review domain scores** — Check that domain-level scores logically follow from the individual question ratings\n**Assess overall result** — Confirm the overall assessment result (Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory/Deficient) accurately reflects the vendor's posture\n**Approve** if all checks pass — the assessment accurately and completely evaluates the vendor's risk\n**Reject** if any checks fail — provide specific comments identifying the gaps so the assessor can address them\nIncomplete responses are the most common reason for rejection — check that all questions are fully answered\nMissing evidence is the second most common issue — especially for high-risk domains\nA compliance rating of 'Satisfactory' with no supporting evidence should be questioned\nWhen in doubt, reject with a request for clarification rather than approving an uncertain assessment\nYour approval means the assessment is the official record — ensure you are confident in its accuracy\napprove\nreject\ncriteria\nchecklist\nquality\ndecision\ncompleteness\naccuracy\nevidence\ncompliance rating	{0.021331787109375,0.0308685302734375,0.06280517578125,0.0205841064453125,-0.005123138427734375,-0.01522064208984375,-0.0277099609375,-0.054534912109375,0.022796630859375,0.08343505859375,0.10418701171875,-0.04266357421875,-0.05157470703125,0.00321197509765625,0.035919189453125,-0.032318115234375,0.0114288330078125,-0.00926971435546875,-0.0114288330078125,0.0181121826171875,0.037384033203125,-0.006351470947265625,0.0089874267578125,0.007183074951171875,-0.0113525390625,-0.0270538330078125,-0.0180511474609375,-0.01255035400390625,0.009735107421875,-0.03570556640625,0.0287322998046875,-0.01271820068359375,-0.021881103515625,0.0162811279296875,-0.044036865234375,-0.005191802978515625,-0.0077056884765625,0.0005707740783691406,0.005939483642578125,-0.0298614501953125,0.006214141845703125,0.036529541015625,-0.00949859619140625,0.0155029296875,-0.025787353515625,0.005016326904296875,0.017120361328125,-0.04840087890625,-0.0277252197265625,-0.0264434814453125,-0.03045654296875,0.055999755859375,0.033966064453125,0.01158905029296875,0.006103515625,0.016510009765625,-0.0156402587890625,0.017822265625,-0.054534912109375,0.0210113525390625,-0.0005970001220703125,-0.0100860595703125,-0.00714111328125,0.0256195068359375,-0.01027679443359375,-0.039520263671875,-0.01442718505859375,-0.0046844482421875,0.0384521484375,-0.00902557373046875,0.0234527587890625,0.0482177734375,0.072265625,0.029815673828125,0.00855255126953125,-0.028778076171875,0.07318115234375,0.042755126953125,-0.0243682861328125,0.007747650146484375,-0.041412353515625,0.038055419921875,-0.01335906982421875,-0.047271728515625,9.894371032714844e-05,0.005046844482421875,-0.070556640625,-0.01375579833984375,-0.0216217041015625,-0.0307159423828125,-0.0289764404296875,0.057769775390625,-0.03265380859375,-0.011993408203125,-0.0247344970703125,0.