cmn2wad6800cxjc3o8lu7njpy	tam-role-overview	tprm	Role Overview	tprm	{AccountManager}	What is the TPRM Account Manager role?	What is the TPRM Account Manager role?\nWhat can I do as an Account Manager?\nAccount Manager role overview\nWhat pages can an Account Manager access in TPRM?\nWhat is the Account Manager responsible for?\nAccount Manager capabilities in TPRM\nWhat does the TPRM Account Manager do?\nAM role summary\nThe TPRM Account Manager manages vendor accounts from a commercial perspective. You handle active assessments (start, resume, offboard), track follow-up actions, and manage Subject Matter Expert (SME) domain assignments — all focused on the vendor-facing side of the assessment lifecycle.\n**AM Assessments** — View assessments across 4 tabs (Active, Submitted, Past, Offboard), start Draft assessments, resume In Progress ones, and route to offboard questionnaires\n**AM Follow-Ups** — Track and manage follow-up actions arising from assessments and reviews, monitor completion status and due dates\n**AM SME Management** — List, assign, and manage Subject Matter Experts for assessment domains, track SME availability and expertise areas\n**AM Support** — Submit support requests for vendor-related queries and access help resources\nThis is a commercially focused role — you manage the vendor relationship side of assessments rather than conducting technical evaluations\nYou can start (Draft) or resume assessments but cannot conduct the CAIQ questionnaire — that is the Assessor's responsibility\nYou have access to only 4 areas: Assessments, Follow-Ups, SME Management, and Support\nAssessment status colors help you quickly identify where each assessment stands: Gray (Draft), Blue (In Progress), Orange (Returned), Purple (Submitted), Indigo (Under Review), Green (Completed)\nUse the search bar on Assessments to quickly find assessments by code or vendor name\naccount manager\nam\nrole\noverview\nresponsibilities\ncapabilities\naccess\ncommercial\nvendor\nassessm