cmn2wadi600d9jc3oss6r6oea	taud-issues	tprm	Issue & Remediation	tprm	{TPRMAuditor}	How do I review the issue register as an Auditor?	How do I review the issue register as an Auditor?\nHow do I audit vendor issues?\nAuditor issue register access\nWhere can I see issue severity breakdown?\nHow to review remediation status as Auditor?\nCan I view issues by vendor as Auditor?\nTPRM Auditor issue tracking\nHow to audit issue resolution?\nThe Issue Register (Assessor view) provides read-only access to all assessment issues grouped by vendor with severity breakdowns (High/Medium/Low). You can drill into vendor-specific issues to review details, remediation status, and resolution progress for audit purposes.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Assessor → Issue Register**\nReview the issue register tab showing vendors grouped with **High/Medium/Low severity counts** and totals\nClick on a vendor to drill into their **detailed issues list**\nFor each issue, review: **domain**, **severity**, **issue description**, **risk**, and **recommendation**\nCheck the **issue status** — Open, Overdue, or Closed — to assess remediation timeliness\nReview the **assessment code linkage** to trace issues back to specific assessments\nCheck **due dates** to identify overdue remediation items\nReview **question number references** to link issues to specific CAIQ questions\nReview any **remediation comments** for adequacy of response\nYou have READ-ONLY access — you cannot create, edit, close, or comment on issues\nIssue statuses: Open (active), Overdue (past due date), Closed (resolved)\nSeverity levels: High, Medium, Low — use these to prioritize audit focus on critical issues\nThe issue register is a key audit artifact — review it to assess whether identified risks are being remediated in a timely manner\nIssues are linked to specific CAIQ questions and assessment codes for traceability\nCompare issue counts and severities across vendors to identify systemic patterns\nissue\nregister\nseverity\nr