cmn2wadil00dajc3odgn4nl1v	taud-monitoring	tprm	Monitoring & Scanning	tprm	{TPRMAuditor}	How do I review vendor monitoring as an Auditor?	How do I review vendor monitoring as an Auditor?\nHow do I view vendor security scores as an Auditor?\nAuditor monitoring scorecard access\nWhere can I see vendor KPI data for audit?\nHow to audit vendor security monitoring?\nCan I view scan results as an Auditor?\nTPRM Auditor monitoring page\nHow to review vendor security posture?\nThe Monitoring page provides read-only access to the vendor security scorecard with 14 KPIs, scan results, and security posture data. You can review vendor security scores and KPI breakdowns for independent audit assessment of the organization's vendor monitoring program.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Monitoring**\nReview the **stat cards** at the top: Vendors Monitored, Avg Security Score, High Risk Vendors, Active Scans\nReview the **Vendor Scorecard table** with sticky vendor name column and 14 KPI columns\nCheck KPI scores across: Network Security, DNS Health, Patching Cadence, Endpoint Security, IP Reputation, Application Security, Cubit Score, Email Security, SSL/TLS Config, Privacy, Known Breach, Hacker Chatter, Information Leak, Social Engineering\nReview the **Security Score badge** per vendor — color-coded by risk level\nNote KPI cell colors: **Green** (score ≥80), **Emerald** (≥65), **Yellow** (≥50), **Red** (<50)\nClick on a vendor to view the **detailed KPI breakdown** and historical scan data\nOnly completed assessments appear in the scorecard — verify scan coverage is adequate\nYou have VIEW-ONLY access — you cannot trigger new scans or delete monitoring records\nThe scorecard provides a quantitative view of vendor security posture across 14 standardized KPIs\nMonitoring scans use AI-powered web intelligence gathering with 17+ targeted searches per vendor\nUse this page to audit whether the organization's vendor monitoring program has adequate coverage and frequency\nCompare security scores over time (via scan history) to assess whether vendors are improving or degrading\nHigh Risk Vendors stat card highlights vendors requiring immediate audit attention\nmonitoring\nsecurity\nscan\nscorecard\nkpi\nnetwork\ndns\nssl\nscore\nvendor\naudit\nposture\nreview	{-0.03704833984375,0.036834716796875,0.065673828125,0.00585174560546875,-0.007228851318359375,-0.0005140304565429688,-0.0457763671875,-0.00643157958984375,0.023681640625,-0.0002132654190063477,0.0106353759765625,-0.043609619140625,-0.01074981689453125,-0.001950263977050781,0.048126220703125,-0.034820556640625,-0.007205963134765625,0.0102691650390625,-0.03680419921875,0.0521240234375,0.058990478515625,0.040008544921875,-0.00908660888671875,-0.002153396606445312,-0.04541015625,0.005573272705078125,-0.0311126708984375,-0.02001953125,0.00736236572265625,-0.0154571533203125,0.0263214111328125,-0.03363037109375,0.0082855224609375,0.026611328125,-0.0187530517578125,0.00238800048828125,-0.0275421142578125,-0.01861572265625,0.01213836669921875,-0.001605033874511719,0.003667831420898438,0.05670166015625,-0.0076446533203125,0.05328369140625,0.01316070556640625,0.01241302490234375,-0.0042572021484375,-0.0228118896484375,-0.0149078369140625,-0.0294189453125,-0.038421630859375,0.047088623046875,-0.01019287109375,-0.002321243286132812,-0.01165008544921875,0.0062255859375,0.00171661376953125,0.01171112060546875,-0.03863525390625,0.020904541015625,0.009185791015625,-0.010772705078125,-0.0193634033203125,-0.0208282470703125,0.01151275634765625,-0.01351165771484375,-0.03326416015625,0.0224456787109375,0.0223541259765625,-0.035736083984375,0.02447509765625,0.0408935546875,0.033782958984375,0.005680084228515625,0.0189208984375,0.0006990432739257812,0.04876708984375,0.0166168212890625,-0.023406982421875,0.0225982666015625,0.0102386474609375,-0.00374603271484375,-0.03271484375,0.0212249755859375,-0.0002131462097167969,-0.0210418701171875,-0.06634521484375,-0.015838623046875,0.026092529296875,0.031005859375,-0.0146026611