cmn2wadrw00dfjc3o1a5by7yd	tsme-role-overview	tprm	Role Overview	tprm	{TPRMSME}	What is the TPRM Subject Matter Expert (SME) role?	What is the TPRM Subject Matter Expert (SME) role?\nWhat can an SME do in TPRM?\nSME role permissions\nWhat pages can the Subject Matter Expert access?\nWhat is the scope of the SME role?\nTPRM SME responsibilities\nHow does the SME role differ from the Account Manager?\nWhat does a Subject Matter Expert do in vendor assessments?\nThe TPRM Subject Matter Expert (SME) is a specialist advisory role that provides domain-specific expertise during vendor assessments. SMEs review specific assessment areas related to their area of specialization and have limited access to three pages: AM Assessments, AM Follow-Ups, and AM Support.\nLog in with your SME credentials to access the TPRM module\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → AM → Assessments** to review assessments assigned to your domain of expertise\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → AM → Follow-Ups** to track follow-up items assigned to you\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → AM → Support** to access help resources and submit support requests\nThe SME role has very limited access — only 3 pages are available: AM Assessments, AM Follow-Ups, and AM Support\nSMEs do NOT have access to dashboards, vendor management, contracts, issues, monitoring, reports, configuration, settings, assessment factory, templates, control center, program monitor, offboarding, SME management, or CAIQ questions\nThis role is designed for specialists who provide expert input on specific assessment domains, not full assessment management\nSMEs are assigned by the Account Manager to review specific areas of vendor assessments\nsme\nsubject matter expert\nrole\npermissions\nspecialist\ndomain expert\nadvisory	{0.00598907470703125,0.052978515625,0.06744384765625,-0.00388336181640625,-0.01277923583984375,0.0164947509765625,0.00635528564453125,0.030517578125,0.04046630859375,0.036956787109375,0.03375244140625,-0.044342041015625,-0.02134