cmn2wae2b00dpjc3olm7tdpzq	tit-it-security-input	tprm	Issue & Remediation	tprm	{InternalITTeam}	How do I provide IT security input for vendor assessments?	How do I provide IT security input for vendor assessments?\nHow to give technical input on vendor issues?\nIT security perspective on vendor risks\nHow does the IT team contribute to vendor assessments?\nProviding infrastructure risk feedback\nTechnology risk input for vendors\nHow to document IT findings on vendor issues?\nAs an Internal IT Team member, you provide technical input on IT-related vendor issues through remediation comments on the IT Issues page. Your expertise covers IT security, infrastructure risks, and technology vulnerabilities identified during vendor assessments.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Internal IT → Issue Management**\nReview issues that require IT security or infrastructure expertise\nAssess the **technical risk** described in each issue from an IT perspective\nEvaluate whether the **recommendation** is technically feasible and sufficient\nAdd **remediation comments** documenting your IT security assessment\nInclude specific technical guidance: security patches, configuration changes, infrastructure upgrades, or control implementations\nFlag any issues where the IT risk is understated or where additional technical controls are needed\nYour IT security input is critical for accurate vendor risk assessment — Assessors and RMs rely on your technical expertise\nFocus areas include: network security, data encryption, access controls, vulnerability management, infrastructure resilience\nIssues are linked to specific assessment domains (e.g., Data Security, Access Control, Business Continuity) for context\nYou do not have access to the full assessment — your input is channeled through the IT Issues page only\nIT security\ntechnical input\ninfrastructure\ntechnology risk\nvendor assessment\nfeedback\nfindings\nsecurity posture	{-0.035247802734375,0.0274810791015625,0.05908203125,0.02862548828