cmn2wae2q00dqjc3obbvjcuri	tit-issue-severity	tprm	Issue & Remediation	tprm	{InternalITTeam}	What do the issue severity levels mean on the IT Issues page?	What do the issue severity levels mean on the IT Issues page?\nHow are IT issues classified by severity?\nWhat is the difference between High, Medium, and Low severity?\nHow to prioritize IT vendor issues?\nIssue severity breakdown for IT team\nUnderstanding High Medium Low issue ratings\nHow are vendor issues categorized?\nIT vendor issues are classified into three severity levels — High, Medium, and Low — indicating the urgency and potential impact of the issue on IT security, infrastructure, or technology risk. High severity issues require immediate IT team attention.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Internal IT → Issue Management**\nReview the **Severity** column for each issue in the list\n**High** severity: Critical IT security or infrastructure risk requiring immediate technical remediation\n**Medium** severity: Significant IT concern that should be addressed within the standard remediation timeline\n**Low** severity: Minor IT-related finding that can be addressed during routine maintenance or next review cycle\nUse severity levels to prioritize your team's remediation efforts — address High issues first\nSeverity is assigned during the assessment process by the Assessor — the IT team reviews from a technical feasibility standpoint\nIssues grouped by vendor show severity breakdowns so you can quickly identify which vendors have the most critical IT issues\nOverdue High severity issues should be flagged immediately as they represent the greatest IT risk to the organization\nSeverity levels align with the organization's risk appetite and TPRM policy thresholds\nseverity\nhigh\nmedium\nlow\npriority\nclassification\ncategorize\nrisk level	{-0.062225341796875,0.0285186767578125,0.057952880859375,0.0174560546875,0.007236480712890625,0.001086235046386719,-0.00507354736328125,-0.0173797607421875,0.0246429443359375,0