cmn2wae3500drjc3oxernmkxq	tit-issue-status	tprm	Issue & Remediation	tprm	{InternalITTeam}	What do the issue statuses mean on the IT Issues page?	What do the issue statuses mean on the IT Issues page?\nWhat does Open, Overdue, and Closed mean for IT issues?\nHow do IT issue statuses work?\nWhen does an IT issue become overdue?\nHow are IT issues closed?\nIssue lifecycle for the Internal IT Team\nUnderstanding IT issue status tracking\nIT issues follow a lifecycle with three statuses: Open (active and within deadline), Overdue (past the remediation due date), and Closed (remediation completed and verified). These statuses help the IT team track remediation progress.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Internal IT → Issue Management**\nCheck the **Status** column for each issue\n**Open**: The issue has been identified and is within its remediation timeline — action is needed from the IT team\n**Overdue**: The issue has passed its due date without being resolved — requires urgent IT attention and possible escalation\n**Closed**: Remediation has been completed and the issue is resolved — no further IT action required\nFilter or sort by status to focus on issues requiring active IT intervention\nOverdue issues are automatically flagged when the current date passes the assigned due date\nThe IT team should prioritize Overdue issues and provide remediation comments explaining delays or blockers\nClosing an issue typically requires verification by the Assessor or Relationship Manager that the remediation is adequate\nDue dates are set during the assessment process — contact the Assessor or RM if a due date extension is needed\nstatus\nopen\noverdue\nclosed\nlifecycle\ntracking\ndue date\nresolution	{-0.02423095703125,0.063720703125,0.059234619140625,-0.006000518798828125,-0.01020050048828125,-0.01226043701171875,0.01715087890625,-0.01061248779296875,0.0260467529296875,0.042724609375,0.06878662109375,0.0231781005859375,-0.04986572265625,-0.0263214111328125,0.0506591796875,-0.0269