cmn2wae3y00dtjc3of22ozkun	tfa-role-overview	tprm	Role Overview	tprm	{FactoryAssessor}	What is the TPRM Factory Assessor role?	What is the TPRM Factory Assessor role?\nWhat can a Factory Assessor do in TPRM?\nFactory Assessor role permissions\nWhat pages can the Factory Assessor access?\nWhat is the scope of the Factory Assessor role?\nTPRM Factory Assessor responsibilities\nHow does the Factory Assessor role differ from the regular Assessor?\nWhat does a Factory Assessor do in vendor management?\nThe TPRM Factory Assessor is the most limited factory-related role. It is designed for personnel who conduct vendor assessments specific to factory or facility requirements. As a Factory Assessor, you have **read-only** access to **Factory Reports** only — you cannot create, edit, or delete any records.\nLog in with your Factory Assessor credentials to access the TPRM module\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Assessor → Assessment History** to view factory assessment reports\nReview completed factory assessment reports — this is your only accessible page\nAll access is **read-only** — you cannot modify, create, or delete any data\nThe Factory Assessor is the most limited factory role in TPRM — you have access to only **1 page**: Factory Reports (view only)\nYou do NOT have access to: All Dashboards, Vendor Management, Contracts, Assessments pages, Issues, Monitoring, Follow-ups, User Management, Configuration, Settings, Assessment Factory (creation), Templates, SME Management, Offboarding, Control Center, Program Monitor, CAIQ Questions, or TPRM Reports\nYour role is focused exclusively on reviewing factory/facility-specific assessment reports — broader TPRM access is managed by Assessors, Relationship Managers, or Administrators\nIf you need to create or manage assessments, contact your TPRM Administrator to request an elevated role\nfactory assessor\nrole\npermissions\nfactory\nfacility\nassessment\nreports\nread-only\nlimited	{-0.005962371826171875,0.054656982421875,0.05776