cmn2waecu00e0jc3o80fc72g9	tfad-factory-roles	tprm	User Management	tprm	{FactoryAdmin}	What roles can I assign to factory team members?	What roles can I assign to factory team members?\nWhat is the difference between FactoryAdmin and FactoryAssessor?\nFactory role types explained\nWhich roles are available for factory users?\nFactoryAdmin vs FactoryAssessor permissions\nHow do factory roles differ?\nWhat can a FactoryAssessor do compared to FactoryAdmin?\nAs a Factory Administrator, you can assign two roles to factory team members: **FactoryAdmin** (full factory administration including user management, assessment factory, and reports) and **FactoryAssessor** (read-only access to factory reports only). Choose the appropriate role based on each team member's responsibilities.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Factory → User Management**\nWhen adding or editing a user, select from the available roles:\n**FactoryAdmin** — Can manage factory users, operate the assessment factory, and view factory reports (3 pages)\n**FactoryAssessor** — Can only view factory assessment reports in read-only mode (1 page)\nAssign **FactoryAdmin** to team leads or deputies who need to manage the factory team and create assessments\nAssign **FactoryAssessor** to team members who only need to review completed assessment reports\nFactoryAdmin is the broader factory role with access to 3 pages: Factory User Management, Assessment Factory, and Factory Reports\nFactoryAssessor is the most limited factory role with read-only access to only 1 page: Factory Reports\nNeither role has access to organization-wide TPRM pages such as dashboards, vendor management, contracts, monitoring, or configuration\nIf a team member needs broader TPRM access beyond the factory scope, contact your TPRM Administrator to assign a different role\nfactory admin\nfactory assessor\nrole\nassign\npermissions\ndifference\nteam\nfacility	{-0.01610065810382366,0.03905878216028214,0.0433027371764183,-0.01134718675166368,-0.002615