cmn2waed800e1jc3ogrrxj6oa	tfad-assessment-factory	tprm	Assessment Management	tprm	{FactoryAdmin}	How do I use the Assessment Factory to batch-create assessments?	How do I use the Assessment Factory to batch-create assessments?\nHow to create multiple assessments at once\nBatch assessment creation for factory\nAssessment Factory page explained\nHow to schedule batch assessments for my factory\nMulti-vendor assessment initiation\nHow does the assessment factory work?\nTemplate-based batch assessment creation\nHow to generate assessments at scale for my factory?\nThe Assessment Factory enables you to batch-create and schedule assessments for multiple vendors at once, specific to your factory/facility. Instead of creating assessments one by one, you can generate them at scale using templates — streamlining the assessment workflow for your factory team.\nNavigate to **Sidebar → TPRM → Assessor → Assessment Factory**\nSelect the vendors you want to assess from the available vendor list\nChoose the assessment template to apply to the batch\nConfigure assessment parameters (type, due dates, assigned assessors)\nReview the batch configuration summary before generating\nClick **Generate** or **Create Batch** to initiate the batch assessment creation\nThe system will create individual assessments for each selected vendor based on your configuration\nMonitor the batch creation status on the page\nThe Assessment Factory is designed for efficiency — use it when you need to create assessments for multiple vendors simultaneously\nAssessments created through the factory follow the same lifecycle as individually created assessments: Draft → In Progress → Submitted → Under Review → Approved/Completed\nTemplate-based creation ensures consistency across all assessments in the batch\nYour factory scope determines which vendors and assessors are available for selection\nBatch creation history is available on the Factory Reports page for audit and tracking purposes\nassessment factory\nbat