cmn5pj4n701dq3u7u8t9wbysk	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Indian Computer Emergency Response Team (CERT-In), Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) — Directions under Section 70B(6) of the Information Technology Act, 2000 (CERT-In Directions), 2022 (effective 28 June 2022)	Regulation	Mandatory	Applies to all service providers, intermediaries, data centres, body corporates and government organisations in India. An IT & software company operating online in India must comply with incident reporting timelines, log retention (180 days), time synchronization, and cooperation/assistance requirements.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e63u7uhzkk35jk	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	ISO/IEC 27701:2019 — Privacy Information Management System (PIMS) extension to ISO/IEC 27001/27002	Standard	Recommended	Supports systematic privacy governance and controls for personal data processing. Useful to operationalize compliance with India’s DPDP Act, 2023 and to meet enterprise customer privacy assurance expectations.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dr3u7u5n26l996	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology Act, 2000 (Act No. 21 of 2000), as amended by the Information Technology (Amendment) Act, 2008	Law/Regulation	Mandatory	Core cyber law for India governing offences, intermediary liability, and government powers for interception/monitoring. Directly applicable to an IT & software private limited company operating digital services and systems in India.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701ds3u7ulaoctp9g	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (Reasonable Security Practices and Procedures and Sensitive Personal Data or Information) Rules, 2011 (under the Information Technology Act, 2000)	Regulation	Mandatory	Imposes legally enforceable requirements on 'body corporates' in India for protecting Sensitive Personal Data or Information (SPDI), including security practices, privacy policy, consent, and grievance handling. Applicable if the company processes employee/user SPDI in India.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dt3u7uy0s1r4tu	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021 (as amended) (under the Information Technology Act, 2000)	Regulation	Mandatory	Applies if the company provides intermediary services (e.g., hosting, search, social platforms, messaging, cloud services) in India. Sets due diligence, grievance redressal, takedown/notice handling, and compliance officer obligations for intermediaries.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701du3u7ubfj9zcf3	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (The Indian Computer Emergency Response Team and Manner of Performing Functions and Duties) Rules, 2013	Regulation	Mandatory	Establishes CERT-In’s functions and the compliance expectations for entities in India interacting with CERT-In. Relevant because CERT-In is the national incident response authority and its directions/requests are binding in practice.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dv3u7u65v7zw1d	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (Act No. 22 of 2023)	Law/Regulation	Mandatory	India’s enacted personal data protection law governing processing of digital personal data, consent/notice, data principal rights, security safeguards, breach notification (as prescribed), and obligations for significant data fiduciaries (if designated). Applicable to an IT & software company processing personal data in India.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dw3u7ulx6eqcws	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (Procedure and Safeguards for Interception, Monitoring and Decryption of Information) Rules, 2009	Regulation	Mandatory	Legally governs how Indian authorities may require interception/monitoring/decryption and the safeguards around such directions. Relevant to IT & software providers operating networks/platforms that may receive lawful orders.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dx3u7uchygpsoa	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (Procedure and Safeguards for Monitoring and Collecting Traffic Data or Information) Rules, 2009	Regulation	Mandatory	Provides the legal framework for monitoring/collection of traffic data by authorised agencies. Applicable to service providers/platform operators in India that may be required to enable/assist such collection under lawful process.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dy3u7ul112y4ah	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (Procedure and Safeguards for Blocking for Access of Information by Public) Rules, 2009	Regulation	Mandatory	Governs blocking orders for online content in India and the process/safeguards. Relevant if the company operates online services, platforms, or hosting that could receive blocking directions.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701dz3u7uxlvaxabm	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Information Technology (Guidelines for Cyber Cafes) Rules, 2011	Regulation	Mandatory	Applicable only if the company operates cyber cafes in India. Included as a conditional mandatory requirement tied to the IT & software sector when providing public internet access services under the definition of a cyber cafe.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e03u7udun4v5o1	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Indian Penal Code, 1860 (Act No. 45 of 1860) — provisions commonly invoked for cyber-enabled offences (e.g., cheating, forgery) (as applicable until replaced in force by new criminal codes for relevant conduct)	Law	Mandatory	Cyber incidents often trigger IPC offences alongside IT Act provisions (e.g., fraud, impersonation, forgery). Relevant to an IT & software company for incident response, investigations, and legal exposure in India.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e13u7ugsfynm6j	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (Act No. 2 of 1974) — investigation/search/seizure and procedural powers relevant to cybercrime	Law	Mandatory	Procedural law used by law enforcement for cybercrime investigations, including seizure of devices/logs and requests for information. Relevant to an IT & software company that may be subject to lawful investigations and evidence preservation.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e23u7ug484lmqu	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	Indian Evidence Act, 1872 (Act No. 1 of 1872) — Section 65B (electronic evidence)	Law	Mandatory	Sets admissibility requirements for electronic records and certificates, impacting logging, evidence handling, and incident forensics. Relevant to an IT & software company for litigation readiness and cyber incident evidence management.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e33u7ujth8ke2z	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	National Critical Information Infrastructure Protection Centre (NCIIPC), Government of India — Directions/requirements under Section 70 of the Information Technology Act, 2000 (applicable if designated as a 'Protected System' / CII entity)	Regulation	Mandatory	Mandatory only if the organisation is notified as part of Critical Information Infrastructure or operates a 'Protected System'. Included as conditional because large-scale cloud/platform providers can be designated; if designated, NCIIPC directives become binding.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e43u7ugvzrgk5h	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	ISO/IEC 27001:2022 — Information Security Management Systems (ISMS) Requirements	Standard	Recommended	Widely accepted baseline for establishing and certifying an ISMS for IT & software organisations. Helps demonstrate 'reasonable security practices' and structured controls aligned to Indian legal expectations (e.g., IT Act SPDI Rules) and enterprise customer requirements.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e53u7u3p26is3r	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	ISO/IEC 27002:2022 — Information security, cybersecurity and privacy protection controls	Standard	Recommended	Provides detailed control guidance to implement an ISMS and operational security program. Particularly relevant for large software/service providers managing complex environments, third parties, and cloud operations.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e73u7upwypbt2g	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0 (2024)	Framework/Standard	Recommended	Globally recognized framework for cybersecurity risk management and maturity across Identify/Protect/Detect/Respond/Recover/Govern. Fits IT & software organisations with large-scale products/services and helps structure controls and metrics.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e83u7uskr7z2z8	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 (Security and Privacy Controls for Information Systems and Organizations)	Framework/Standard	Recommended	Comprehensive control catalog suitable for large technology organisations and cloud/service providers. Helps map controls to legal obligations (incident response, logging, access control) and customer assurance requirements.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701e93u7u1i4lsial	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	CIS Critical Security Controls v8	Framework/Standard	Recommended	Actionable prioritized controls that align well with common attack patterns and CERT-In expectations (logging, incident response, vulnerability management). Useful for operational hardening across endpoints, cloud, and enterprise IT.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701ea3u7unqmbuhzo	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	ISO/IEC 27017:2015 — Code of practice for information security controls for cloud services	Standard	Recommended	Directly relevant if the organisation provides or consumes cloud services as part of IT & software operations. Strengthens shared responsibility, tenant isolation, and cloud-specific control implementation.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701eb3u7ucquwk6px	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	ISO/IEC 27018:2019 — Protection of PII in public clouds acting as PII processors	Standard	Recommended	Relevant for cloud/service operations handling customer personal data. Helps demonstrate privacy safeguards and contractual/operational controls expected by enterprise customers and regulators.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701ec3u7ugceqhrz0	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	SOC 2 (AICPA Trust Services Criteria, 2017; reporting periods current) — Type II attestation	Standard/Assurance Framework	Recommended	Commonly required by enterprise customers for IT & software/SaaS providers to evidence security, availability, confidentiality, processing integrity, and privacy controls. Supports market access and assurance for services operated in India.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701ed3u7uuftz4tzo	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	OWASP Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) (latest stable version)	Framework/Standard	Recommended	Directly relevant to software development and secure SDLC for an IT & software company. Provides testable security requirements for web/mobile/API applications to reduce vulnerabilities and support compliance-by-design.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
cmn5pj4n701ee3u7us3v6rp5r	cmn31d1b500esjc3oubbjw7fb	cmn5phzbw01cf3u7uddd50kcy	ISO/IEC 27005:2022 — Information security risk management	Framework/Guideline	Optional	Provides structured risk assessment and treatment methods to complement ISO/IEC 27001. Useful for scaling risk governance across products, engineering, and operations in a large IT & software organisation.	\N	f	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603	2026-03-25 07:13:37.603
