cmn2ufco701eczkpvl8mx5ycj	ISS-001	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2ueqxl01aszkpvp59thwgw	IS-01	Does your organization enforce data encryption for all data at rest using industry-standard algorithms (e.g., AES-256)?	No	Information Security	High	\N	Vendor does not enforce AES-256 encryption on all storage systems. Legacy databases remain unencrypted, exposing sensitive client data to unauthorized access.	Unencrypted data at rest can be exfiltrated if storage is compromised, leading to regulatory fines (GDPR, PCI-DSS) and reputational damage.	Mandate full-disk encryption with AES-256 across all storage tiers. Implement key management via HSM. Target completion within 90 days.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-01 00:00:00	2026-04-15 00:00:00	\N	\N	RM please review and coordinate with the vendor for remediation timeline.	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:20.934	Open	2026-03-23 07:07:20.936	2026-03-23 07:07:20.936
cmn2ufd2x01eezkpvrv361w64	ISS-002	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2ueqxl01aszkpvp59thwgw	IS-02	Does the vendor implement multi-factor authentication (MFA) for all user access to critical systems?	Partial	Information Security	Critical	\N	MFA is only enabled for admin accounts. Regular user accounts on production systems rely solely on passwords, increasing the risk of credential-based attacks.	Single-factor authentication on production systems creates a high-risk attack vector. Compromised credentials could lead to unauthorized data access and lateral movement.	Deploy MFA for all user accounts accessing production environments. Consider FIDO2/WebAuthn for phishing-resistant authentication.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-28 00:00:00	2026-03-30 00:00:00	\N	\N	Critical finding - needs immediate attention from RM.	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:21.464	Pending	2026-03-23 07:07:21.466	2026-03-23 07:07:21.466
cmn2ufdcm01egzkpvmd1utisd	ISS-003	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uerbz01auzkpvifybiojz	CS-01	Does the cloud service provider guarantee data residency within contracted geographic boundaries?	Yes	Cloud Security	Medium	\N	While data residency is contractually guaranteed, monitoring and audit mechanisms to verify compliance are not automated. Manual checks are performed quarterly.	Without continuous monitoring, data could inadvertently be processed outside contracted regions during failover events, creating regulatory non-compliance.	Implement automated data residency monitoring using cloud-native tools (e.g., Azure Policy). Set up real-time alerts for cross-region data transfers.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-05 00:00:00	2026-05-01 00:00:00	\N	\N	Please verify with Azure team about their monitoring capabilities.	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:21.812	Open	2026-03-23 07:07:21.814	2026-03-23 07:07:21.814
cmn2ufdm201eizkpvnx7vcgmt	ISS-004	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2ues6t01b0zkpvi05d2khr	RM-01	Has the vendor updated their risk register to reflect the current threat landscape including emerging AI-based threats?	No	Risk Management	High	\N	IBM's vendor risk register has not been updated since Q2 2025. It does not account for AI-driven threats, supply chain attacks, or zero-day exploit trends observed in H2 2025.	Outdated risk register may result in unmitigated threats. The organization may not be adequately prepared for emerging attack vectors targeting AI/ML pipelines.	Request immediate update of vendor risk register. Include AI threat modeling, supply chain risk assessment, and zero-day response procedures.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-08 00:00:00	2026-04-01 00:00:00	\N	\N	Annual review flagged this. RM to follow up with IBM security team.	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:22.152	Open	2026-03-23 07:07:22.154	2026-03-23 07:07:22.154
cmn2ufdvi01ekzkpv9umqglzv	ISS-005	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uesga01b2zkpviwy7dvhj	ERP-01	Are user access reviews conducted at least quarterly with evidence of remediation for identified access violations?	Partial	ERP Security	Medium	\N	SAP user access reviews are conducted quarterly, but remediation of identified violations takes an average of 45 days. Three privilege escalation findings from Q4 2025 remain unresolved.	Delayed remediation of access violations creates a window for privilege abuse. SOD conflicts may persist, increasing the risk of fraudulent transactions.	Enforce a 15-day SLA for remediation of access review findings. Implement automated SOD conflict detection and integrate with SAP GRC Access Control.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-02 00:00:00	2026-04-20 00:00:00	\N	\N	\N	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:22.493	Pending	2026-03-23 07:07:22.495	2026-03-23 07:07:22.495
cmn2ufe5001emzkpvaw53fsy1	ISS-006	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uet8x01b8zkpvcgqhalwg	DB-01	Is encryption at rest enabled for all database instances, including legacy and development environments?	No	Database Security	Critical	\N	Oracle legacy database systems (versions 12c and earlier) do not have TDE (Transparent Data Encryption) enabled. Development environments contain production data copies without any encryption.	Unencrypted production data in development environments violates data protection regulations. Legacy systems are vulnerable to data exfiltration through physical media theft or unauthorized backup access.	Enable TDE on all Oracle instances immediately. Mask or anonymize production data used in development. Upgrade legacy 12c instances to 19c with encryption enabled by default.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-20 00:00:00	2026-03-25 00:00:00	\N	\N	Database security is critical. RM coordinate with Oracle team for emergency remediation.	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:22.834	Open	2026-03-23 07:07:22.836	2026-03-23 07:07:22.836
cmn2ufeed01eozkpvlj1all05	ISS-007	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2ueub401bgzkpvqsfgcbpt	ERP-03	Has custom ABAP code been reviewed for security vulnerabilities using static analysis tools?	No	ERP Security	High	\N	Custom ABAP code deployed across 12 SAP modules has never been subjected to static code analysis. Preliminary manual review found SQL injection patterns and hardcoded credentials in 3 custom programs.	Vulnerable custom code in production SAP systems could be exploited for data theft, privilege escalation, or system manipulation. Hardcoded credentials pose an immediate security risk.	Conduct comprehensive ABAP code scan using SAP Code Vulnerability Analyzer or third-party tools (e.g., Virtual Forge). Remediate critical findings within 30 days. Establish mandatory code review process for all custom developments.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-05 00:00:00	2026-04-10 00:00:00	\N	\N	\N	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:23.171	Open	2026-03-23 07:07:23.173	2026-03-23 07:07:23.173
cmn2ufenx01eqzkpvg0f6pef1	ISS-008	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uerbz01auzkpvifybiojz	CO-01	Does the vendor maintain current SOC 2 Type II certification with no critical exceptions noted?	Yes	Compliance	Low	\N	SOC 2 Type II report is current but contains two minor exceptions related to change management notification delays. While classified as low risk, the exceptions indicate process gaps.	Minor SOC 2 exceptions, if not addressed, could escalate to material findings in future audits, potentially affecting the vendor's compliance posture.	Request vendor's remediation plan for the two SOC 2 exceptions. Monitor resolution progress in the next assessment cycle.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-10 00:00:00	2026-06-01 00:00:00	\N	\N	\N	cmn2uezpr01d8zkpvhl4hv9st	2026-03-23 07:07:23.515	Pending	2026-03-23 07:07:23.517	2026-03-23 07:07:23.517
cmn2ufzmz01gozkpv38wpeg5m	ISS-IT-001	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2ueqxl01aszkpvp59thwgw	BC-02	Does the vendor maintain a comprehensive Business Continuity Plan covering all critical services?	No	Business Continuity	Medium	\N	BCP gaps identified for 3 critical IT services. Internal IT team needs to verify vendor BCP alignment with our infrastructure dependencies.	IT service dependencies on vendor may be unprotected during major incidents, leading to extended downtime.	IT team to map vendor BCP gaps against internal infrastructure dependencies and validate failover procedures.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-01 00:00:00	2026-05-01 00:00:00	\N	\N	Assigned to IT team for infrastructure dependency validation.	cmn2uf9e401e2zkpvc7br7v0l	2026-03-23 07:07:50.698	Assigned to IT	2026-03-23 07:07:50.7	2026-03-23 07:07:50.7
cmn2ug01l01gqzkpv17tvtadw	ISS-IT-002	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uerbz01auzkpvifybiojz	CS-03	Does the cloud provider implement automated encryption key rotation for all services?	Partial	Cloud Security	High	\N	Azure key rotation is manual. IT team needs to configure and test automated key rotation in Azure Key Vault for our tenant.	Manual key rotation delays create a window of vulnerability. Compromised keys may remain active longer than security policy allows.	Configure automated key rotation policies in Azure Key Vault. Test rotation procedures in staging environment before production deployment.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-05 00:00:00	2026-04-15 00:00:00	\N	\N	IT team to implement automated key rotation in our Azure tenant.	cmn2uf9e401e2zkpvc7br7v0l	2026-03-23 07:07:51.223	Assigned to IT	2026-03-23 07:07:51.225	2026-03-23 07:07:51.225
cmn2ug0b401gszkpvnrvaujti	ISS-IT-003	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uet8x01b8zkpvcgqhalwg	DB-01	Does the vendor implement encryption for all databases including legacy systems?	No	Database Security	Critical	\N	Oracle legacy databases lack encryption. IT team must implement compensating controls until vendor completes encryption migration.	Unencrypted legacy databases expose sensitive data. Any breach could result in regulatory penalties and data loss.	Implement network-level encryption (TLS) for all Oracle database connections. Deploy database activity monitoring as compensating control.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	/uploads/tprm/it-remediation/oracle-tls-config.pdf	Oracle_Network_TLS_Config.pdf	2026-02-25 00:00:00	2026-03-30 00:00:00	\N	\N	Critical: IT team to implement compensating controls immediately.	cmn2uf9e401e2zkpvc7br7v0l	2026-03-23 07:07:51.567	Assigned to IT	2026-03-23 07:07:51.569	2026-03-23 07:07:51.569
cmn2ug0kq01guzkpv86ha73bx	ISS-IT-004	grc-admin-account-1	cmn2uevw201bszkpvjt3junk3	IT-02	Does the vendor track and report on Service Level Agreement (SLA) performance metrics systematically?	No	IT Outsourcing	High	\N	Wipro lacks systematic SLA tracking. IT team needs to set up internal monitoring to independently track vendor SLA performance.	Without independent SLA monitoring, service degradation may go undetected, impacting business operations.	Deploy SLA monitoring dashboard using existing monitoring tools. Configure alerts for SLA threshold breaches.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-03-10 00:00:00	2026-04-30 00:00:00	\N	\N	IT team to set up independent SLA monitoring for Wipro services.	cmn2uf9e401e2zkpvc7br7v0l	2026-03-23 07:07:51.913	Assigned to IT	2026-03-23 07:07:51.914	2026-03-23 07:07:51.914
